hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21601","1003 - Allan ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ilyas, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would wake up in janabah, then fast that day."
"21602","1004 - And with his chain she said: I and the Messenger of Allah would bathe from a single vessel."
"21603","A'ishah from Umm Salamah. 1005 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Abdullah ibn Sa'd al-Ayli, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Umm Ruman, from A'ishah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said with me one day, then woke with his eyes red, and his head shook: Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. I said: What is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: There has been opened of the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj like this - and he made ten with a knot. She said: I do not know whether like the ring or like the fingertip. I said: Do you fear destruction for us, O Messenger of Allah, while the righteous are among us? He said: Yes, when filth increases. Umm Ruman said: A'ishah said: I asked the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - about this hadith, and he narrated it to me as Umm Salamah said."
"21604","Umm Hakim bint Abi Umayyah from Umm Salamah. 1006 - Abu Bakr ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Sulayman ibn Suhaym narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Hakim bint Abi Umayyah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever enters ihram for Umrah from Bayt al-Maqdis will be forgiven."
"21605","Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd from Umm Salamah. 1007 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nafi', from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, from Umm Salamah, that when the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - mentioned about the waist-wrapper what he mentioned, Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of Allah, what about women? He said: Let them lower a span. She said: Then their feet will show. He said: Then a cubit, and let them not exceed it."
"21606","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Hudbah ibn Khalid, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said about the train of the garment what he said, Umm Salamah said: What about us women? He said: You trail it a span. She said: Then the feet will be exposed. He said: You trail it a cubit."
"21607","The paternal aunt of Abu Bakr ibn Umarah from Umm Salamah. Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Humayd, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Misar, from Abu Bakr ibn Umarah, from his paternal aunt, from Umm Salamah, she said: If one of us performed ghusl she would take care that no one see her yellowness."
"21608","Mawiyah from Umm Salamah. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Abu Amir, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from a freedwoman of her father called Mawiyah, that she informed her, that she asked Umm Salamah and said: My eye has become accustomed to kohl that contains perfume, and her husband had died leaving her; is it proper for me to apply kohl? She said: By Allah, I will not command you with anything that Allah and His Messenger forbade."
"21609","Umm Uthman from Umm Salamah. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Abu Amir, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Umm Uthman, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman to mourn more than three days, except a woman for her husband, four months and ten days."
"21610","Khawlah from Umm Salamah. Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman, narrated to us Abu al-Aswad, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Khawlah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not apply perfume while you are in ihram, and do not touch henna, for it is perfume."
"21611","Unnamed women from Umm Salamah. Narrated to us Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas, narrated to us my father, Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn al-Dahhak al-Hizami, he said: Umm Hakim bint Asad informed me, from her mother, from a freedwoman of hers, whom she sent to Umm Salamah, she said: I heard Umm Salamah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me while I was in my waiting period after the death of Abu Salamah: Do not comb with perfume nor with henna, for it is a dye. I said: With what shall I comb, O Messenger of Allah? He said: With lote-tree leaves, you wrap your head with it."
"21612","And from Umm Salamah she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me when Abu Salamah died, and I had put aloes on my eye, so he said: What is this, O Umm Salamah? I said: It is only aloes, O Messenger of Allah, there is no perfume in it. He said: It brightens the face, so apply it at night and remove it in the daytime."
"21613","Narrated to us Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun, Quraysh ibn Hayyan al-Ijli informed us, Amatullah bint Madhur narrated to us, from her mother, she said: I entered upon Umm Salamah while she was praying in a shirt and headcover, so I asked her about the mark on the garment, and she said: We used to wear a garment like this, a garment on it with a mark of silk, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21614","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Awn al-Nili, narrated to us al-Harith ibn Muawiyah ibn al-Harith, from his grandfather, the father of his mother, that he used to say: I have a hadith with me, if I wanted to eat the world with it I could eat it, but may Allah not ask me about a hadith I raise to the ruler. My father said: So I said: What is it? He said: When Zayd came out I came to my maternal aunt the next morning and said to her: O mother, Zayd has come out. She said: The poor man will be killed as his fathers were killed. I said to her: Men of understanding came out with him. She said: I was with Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they mentioned the caliphate, so Umm Salamah said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they mentioned the caliphate after him, and they said: The children of Fatimah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They will never reach it; rather it is among the children of my uncle, the twin of my father, until they hand it over to the Dajjal."
"21615","The wife of Hunaydah from Umm Salamah. Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Said al-Asbahani, (Ha). And narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Abd al-Rahim, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Hurr ibn Sabbah, from Hunaydah ibn Khalid al-Khuzai, from his wife, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Fast three days of every month from its beginning: Monday, and Thursday, and the Thursday that follows it."
"21616","The mother of Ibn Buraydah from Umm Salamah. Narrated to us Bakr, narrated to us Nuaym ibn Hammad, (Ha). And narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, (Ha). And narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Amr al-Wasiti, (Ha). And narrated to us Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi, he said: narrated to us Ali ibn Bahr, they said: narrated to us Abu Tumaylah, from Abd al-Mumin ibn Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: Nothing was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than a shirt."
"21617","Maymunah bint al-Harith, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she is the maternal aunt of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both. Narrated to us Abu Usamah Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani al-Rusafi, narrated to us my grandfather Abdullah ibn Ziyad, from al-Zuhri, he said: Maymunah bint al-Harith ibn Hazn ibn Bujayr ibn al-Harim ibn Ruwaybah ibn Abdullah ibn Hilal ibn Amir ibn Sasah, and she is the one who offered herself to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21618","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib, he said: and narrated to us Abdullah ibn Abdullah al-Umawi, from Abdullah ibn Abi Labid, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Maymunah entrusted her affair to Umm al-Fadl, and Umm al-Fadl entrusted it to al-Abbas, so he married her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21619","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi, narrated to us Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham, narrated to us Ziyad ibn Abdullah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died in the year of al-Harrah, year sixty-three."
"21620","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nuaym, narrated to us Uqbah ibn Wahb ibn Uqbah al-Bakkai, he said: Yazid ibn al-Asamm informed me, he said: I saw Umm al-Muminin Maymunah shaving her head after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I said to Yazid ibn al-Asamm, he said: I think she was being austere."
"21621","What Ibn Abbas narrated from his maternal aunt Maymunah. What Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), transmitted with isnad. Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: I screened the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he performed ghusl from janabah; he began and washed his hands, then poured with his right over his left and washed his private part and what had touched it, then struck his hand on the wall or the ground, then performed wudu as for prayer except his feet, then poured water over himself, then moved his feet aside and washed them."
"21622","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us al-Qanabi, narrated to us Isa ibn Yunus, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: My maternal aunt Maymunah narrated to me, she said: I brought near for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) his ghusl from janabah, so he washed his hand twice or thrice, then put his hands into the vessel and poured with them over his private part and washed it with his left, then struck his left on the ground and rubbed it hard, then performed wudu as for prayer, then poured over his head three handfuls filling his palms, then washed the rest of his body, then moved away from that place and washed his feet, then I brought him a towel and he refused it."
"21623","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Yusuf al-Qadi, they said: narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Dawud, from al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from his maternal aunt Maymunah, she said: I put for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ghusl water to wash from janabah, so he tilted the vessel onto his right hand and washed it twice or thrice, then poured over his private part and washed his private part with his left, then struck his hand on the ground and washed it, then rinsed his mouth and nose and washed his face and hands, then poured over his head and body, then moved aside and washed his feet, then I handed him a towel and he did not take it, and he began shaking the water off his body."
"21624","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, narrated to us Sufyan, narrated to us al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ghusl from janabah and washed his private part, then rubbed it on the wall, then washed it, then performed wudu as for prayer, and when he finished his ghusl he washed his feet."
"21625","Narrated to us Musa ibn Jumhur al-Tinnisi, narrated to us al-Walid ibn Shuja ibn al-Walid, narrated to us my father, narrated to us al-Ruhayl ibn Muawiyah, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: Ghusl water was placed for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he poured with his right over his left until he cleansed it, then poured with his right over his private part and washed it with his left and what had touched it until he cleansed it, then rubbed his hand on the wall, on the dust, then washed it until he cleansed it, then rinsed his mouth and nose and performed wudu as for prayer, then poured over his head and his body, then moved from his place and washed his feet."
"21626","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Nafi, freedman of Ibn Umar, saying: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Mabad narrated to us, that Ibn Abbas narrated to him, that Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A prayer in this mosque of mine is a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the mosque of the Kabah."
"21627","Narrated to us al-Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Salih, al-Layth narrated to me, from Nafi, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Mabad, from Ibn Abbas, that Maymunah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A prayer in it - meaning his mosque - is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere among the mosques, except the mosque of the Kabah."
"21628","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail, and Muhammad ibn Said al-Asbahani, and Asim ibn Ali, they said: narrated to us Sharik, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: I became junub, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I washed in a basin and some leftover remained, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and washed from it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, some remained from me. He said: Water is not affected by janabah."
"21629","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani, narrated to us Sharik, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: I used to wash, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel."
"21630","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, (Ha). And narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us al-Qanabi, (Ha). And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki and Bakr ibn Sahl, they said: narrated to us Said ibn Mansur, (Ha). And narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, he said: narrated to us al-Humaydi, all of them from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd Abu al-Shatha, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: I used to wash, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel."
"21631","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, he said: My knowledge and what comes to mind is that Abu al-Shatha informed him, that Ibn Abbas informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash with the leftover water of Maymunah."
"21632","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Maymunah narrated to me, that a sheep died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not tan its hide?"
"21633","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, my father narrated to me, narrated to us Rawh ibn Ubadah, narrated to us Shubah, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A sheep belonging to Maymunah died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not tan it, why did you not use it? They said: It is carrion. He said: Tanning the skin is its purification."
"21634","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, narrated to us Sufyan, narrated to us al-Zuhri, Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah informed me, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a sheep belonging to a freedwoman of ours that she had been given from charity, dead, and said: What is wrong with its people if they took its hide and tanned it and benefited from it? They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is carrion. He said: Only eating it was forbidden. It was said to Sufyan that Mamar does not mention in it they tanned it, and says al-Zuhri used to deny tanning, so Sufyan said: But I memorized it, and we only wanted from it this word that others transmitted: only eating it was forbidden."
"21635","Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us al-Qanabi, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep and said: Why did they not strip its hide and tan it and benefit from it? He said: It is carrion. He said: Only eating it was forbidden."
"21636","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep belonging to a freedwoman of Maymunah and said: Why did you not use its hide? They said: How, while it is carrion, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Only its flesh was forbidden."
"21637","Narrated to us Abu Amir Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Nahwi al-Suri, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi, narrated to us Shuayb ibn Ishaq, narrated to us al-Awzai, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep and said: Why did you not benefit from its skin? They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is carrion. He said: Only eating it was forbidden."
"21638","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Amr, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that a sheep died and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about it, so he said: Only its flesh was forbidden to you, and its skin was permitted to you."
"21639","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep and said: Its people were unable to benefit from its hide."
"21640","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Baghdadi, narrated to us Said ibn Dawud al-Zubayri, narrated to us Malik ibn Anas, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee. He said: Take it and what is around it and throw it away, and eat your ghee."
"21641","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, narrated to us Sufyan, narrated to us al-Zuhri, Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah informed me, that he heard Ibn Abbas narrating from Maymunah, that a mouse fell into ghee and died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked and said: Throw it and what is around it away and eat it. Al-Humaydi said: It was said to Sufyan that Mamar narrates it from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, so Sufyan said: I only heard al-Zuhri narrating it from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I heard it from him many times."
"21642","Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us Ali ibn al-Madini, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee, so he said: Throw it and what is around it away and eat it."
"21643","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to me, narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar ibn Budhawayh, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse falling into ghee, so he said: If it is solid, throw it and what is around it away; and if it is liquid, do not approach it."
"21644","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Abdullah al-Kharaqi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Mirdas al-Ansari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Marwan, narrated to us Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah bint al-Harith, Maymunah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up heavy in spirit and remained so in the evening. I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you heavy? He said: Jibril promised to come to me and never broke his promise to me. They looked and there was a puppy under their table, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that puppy to be taken out and ordered that place to be washed with water. Then Jibril came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You promised to come to me and never broke your promise to me. He said: Do you not know that we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image?"
"21645","Narrated to us Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Salih, al-Layth narrated to me, Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq informed me, that Ibn Abbas said: Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke one day silent and grieved. Maymunah said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have disliked your state since today. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril had promised to meet me tonight but did not meet me; by Allah, he never broke his promise to me. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained that day upon that, then a puppy occurred to his mind under a mat of ours, so he ordered it to be taken out, then he took water in his hand and sprinkled his place with it. When evening came Jibril met him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You had promised to meet me last night. He said: Yes, but we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke that day and ordered the killing of dogs, until he ordered the killing of the dog of the large walled garden, and left the dog of the small walled garden."
"21646","Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us Abu al-Walid Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik al-Tayalisi, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Kathir, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day heavy, so I said: Why do I see you heavy? He said: Jibril promised me and never broke his promise to me. He remained his day like that and his night, and with me was a dog under a table of ours, so he ordered it, then took water in his hand and sprinkled its place with it, then Jibril came and said: We do not enter a house in which there is an image or a dog. She said: He was spoken to about the dog of the small walled garden but he did not permit it."
"21647","Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah from Maymunah. Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from al-Amash, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Maymunah, she said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever takes a debt intending to repay it, Allah will pay it off for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"21648","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah ibn Man, narrated to us my father, from al-Amash, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ubaydullah ibn Utbah, he said: Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), took a debt of eight hundred dirhams. It was said to her: Do you borrow when you have nothing to repay? She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever takes a debt while telling himself to repay it, Allah will help him with it."
"21649","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Jarir, from al-Amash, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Maymunah bint al-Harith, she said: A year of drought struck the people, and the Bedouins used to come to Madinah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to order a man to take a man by his hand and host him and give him supper. A Bedouin came one night, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a little food and some milk, so the Bedouin ate it and left nothing for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He brought him a night or two nights and he kept eating it all. I said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Allah, do not bless this Bedouin; he eats the food of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and leaves him. Then he brought him one night, and he ate only a little of the food and drank only a little of the milk. I said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That was he. And he brought him one night after he had become Muslim, and he said: The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine."
"21650","Ali ibn al-Husayn from Maymunah. Narrated to us Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari, narrated to us Yahya ibn Sulayman ibn Nadlah al-Madini, narrated to us my uncle Muhammad ibn Nadlah, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: Maymunah bint al-Harith narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spent the night with her on her night, then stood to perform wudu for prayer, and she heard him saying in his ablution place: At Your service, at Your service, at Your service, three times, and: I was helped, I was helped, three times. She said: When he came out I said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father be ransomed for you, I heard you saying in your ablution place labbayk labbayk three times, nusirtu nusirtu three times, as if you were speaking to a man; was anyone with you? He said: This is the rajiz of Banu Kab seeking my help, claiming that Quraysh helped Banu Bakr against them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and ordered Aishah to prepare him and not inform anyone. She said: Her father came to her and said: O daughter, what is this preparation? She said: By Allah I do not know. He said: This is not the time of raiding Banu al-Asfar, so where does the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intend? She said: I have no knowledge. She said: We stayed three days, then he prayed dawn with the people and I heard the rajiz reciting to him of being wronged, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was helped, three times, or: Labbayk labbayk, three times. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, and when he was at al-Rawha he looked at an upright cloud and said: This cloud rises with the victory of Banu Kab. A man from Banu Nasr ibn Adi ibn Amr, brother of Banu Kab ibn Amr, stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, and the victory of Banu Adi? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dust on your cheek; is Adi but Kab and Kab but Adi? That man was martyred on that journey. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, blind them to our news until we take them by surprise. Then he went out until he camped at Marr, and Abu Sufyan and Hakim ibn Hizam and Budayl ibn Warqa had come out that night and overlooked Marr. Abu Sufyan looked at the fires and said: O Budayl, Banu Kab have withheld their families. He said: War has driven them to you. Then they came down and Muzaynah took them, and they were on guard that night, so they asked them to take them to al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib. They took them, and Abu Sufyan asked him to seek security for him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Abbas brought them to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then came out with them, and Abu Sufyan said: We want to go. He said: Travel by daybreak. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood performing wudu, and the Muslims rushed to his wudu water splashing it on their faces. Abu Sufyan said: O Abu al-Fadl, the kingdom of your nephew has become great. He said: It is not a kingdom but it is prophethood, and in that they desire."
"21651","Yazid ibn al-Asamm, son of the sister of Maymunah, from Maymunah. Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nuaym, narrated to us Jafar ibn Burqan, he said: Yazid ibn al-Asamm narrated to me, from Maymunah bint al-Harith, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated he kept apart until his back could be seen, and he opened his armpits."
"21652","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, narrated to us Sufyan, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid ibn al-Asamm al-Akbar, from both of them, from his uncle Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymunah, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, if a young sheep wanted to pass under him it could pass, because of his keeping apart."
"21653","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Asamm informed me, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymunah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated he kept apart, so that if a beast wanted to pass under his hands it could pass."
"21654","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Dirar ibn Surad, narrated to us Abdah ibn Sulayman, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Asamm, from his uncle Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymunah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated he kept apart until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen; he leaned on the right and relaxed the left."
"21655","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Jarir, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Yazid al-Asamm, from his maternal aunt Maymunah, that a lizard was gifted to her, then two men of her people came to her, so she ordered it to be prepared, then offered it to them. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while they were eating, and he welcomed them, then took to eat. When he brought the morsel to his mouth he said: What is this? He said: A lizard gifted to us. She said: So he put down the morsel, and the two men wanted to throw what was in their mouths, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not do so; you, people of Najd, eat it, and we, people of Tihamah, find it distasteful."
"21656","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, son of the sister of Maymunah, from Maymunah bint al-Harith, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me at Sarif while we were both lawful."
"21657","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Abi Fazarah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymunah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her while she was lawful."
"21658","Abdullah ibn Salit, foster brother of Maymunah, from Maymunah. Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Yahya ibn Said, from al-Hakam ibn Farrukh Abu Bakkar, from Abi al-Malih ibn Usamah, he said: Abdullah ibn Salit narrated to me, from one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Maymunah, and he was her foster brother, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no Muslim over whom a community prays but they are made intercessors for him. And Abu al-Malih used to say: A community is forty and above."
"21659","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Saib, son of the brother of Maymunah, from Maymunah. Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Salih, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Azhar ibn Said, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Saib al-Hilali, and he is the son of the brother of Maymunah, he said: Maymunah said to me: O son of my brother, shall I charm you with the charm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: In the name of Allah I charm you, and Allah heals you from every disease in you; remove the harm, Lord of men, heal, there is no healer but You."
"21660","Ata ibn Yasar from Maymunah. Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us al-Qanabi, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, he said: Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir informed me, from Ata ibn Yasar, from the Hilaliyyah who was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she had a black slave girl, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to free her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why do you not ransom with her the daughter of your brother or the daughter of your sister from herding sheep?"
"21661","Narrated to us Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi, narrated to us Abu Hudhayfah, narrated to us Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, (Ha). And narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, my father narrated to me, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, narrated to us Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not make nabidh in muzaffat nor in naqir. And every intoxicating drink is forbidden."
"21662","Sulayman ibn Yasar from Maymunah. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Samurah al-Baghdadi, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Yunus ibn Bukayr al-Shaybani, narrated to us my father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: My sister Umm Hufayd gifted me lizards, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned while thinking they were chickens. I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you know what this is? He said: No. Then he held his hand. I said: This is a lizard. He said: That is the food of the Bedouins. Khalid said: Is it forbidden? He said: No. So Khalid ate from it before him while he was looking (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21663","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Uqal al-Harrani, narrated to us Abu Jafar al-Nufayli, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yaqub ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Maymunah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"21664","Narrated to us Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Maymunah, she said: I freed a slave girl of mine, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and I informed him of freeing her. He said: May Allah reward you; had you given her to your maternal uncles it would have been greater for your reward."
"21665","Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah. Narrated to us al-Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Salih, narrated to us al-Layth, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, that Maymunah bint al-Harith informed him, that she freed a slave girl of hers without the permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being sought. When it was her day on which he visited her in turn she said: Did you know, O Messenger of Allah, that I freed my slave girl so-and-so? He said: Have you done so? She said: Yes. He said: Had you given her to your maternal uncles it would have been greater for your reward."
"21666","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Harmalah ibn Yahya, (Ha). And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Dirar ibn Surad, they said: narrated to us Abdullah ibn Wahb, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Kurayb, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder at her house, then prayed and did not perform wudu."
"21667","Miqsam, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah. Narrated to us Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi, narrated to us Amr ibn Marzuq, narrated to us Shubah, from al-Hakam, he said: I asked Miqsam, he said: I said I pray witr with three, then I go out to prayer fearing it will escape me, so he said: It is not proper except with five or seven. So I informed Mujahid and Yahya ibn al-Jazzar of his saying, and they said to me: Did you not ask him from whom? He said: So I asked him and he said: From the trustworthy one, from Maymunah and Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21668","Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Maymunah. Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti, Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us, from al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, he said: Maymunah bint al-Harith, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while I was opposite him, and I was menstruating, and his garment would sometimes touch me when he prostrated."
"21669","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Khalid ibn Abdullah and Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, they said: narrated to us Sulayman al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while I was beside him, and I was menstruating, and his garment would sometimes touch me when he prostrated."
"21670","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Jarir, from al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch his wives while they were menstruating, ordering them to wrap their lower garments."
"21671","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti, Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us, from al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on the khumrah."
"21672","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Khalid ibn Abdullah and Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, they said: narrated to us Sulayman al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on the khumrah."
"21673","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki, narrated to us Said ibn Mansur, narrated to us Hushaym, from al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on the khumrah, and it had been spread for him in the mosque."
"21674","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, (Ha). And narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani, they said: narrated to us Sufyan, narrated to us Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on the khumrah."
"21675","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Khalid ibn Abdullah, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Maymunah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to touch one of his wives while she was menstruating, he ordered her to wrap herself with a waist wrapper, then he touched her."
"21676","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, (Ha). And narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani, they said: narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray with a woolen cloak over him, part of it on him and part of it on one of his wives while she was menstruating. Al-Humaydi said in his hadith: Part of it on me and part of it on him while I was menstruating."
"21677","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while I was sleeping beside him; when he prostrated his garment touched my garment while I was menstruating."
"21678","Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from Amir al-Shabi, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never left my house but he raised his sight to the sky and said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You lest I stray or be led astray, or slip or be made to slip, or be ignorant or be treated ignorantly, or wrong or be wronged."
"21679","Jurayy ibn Samurah from Maymunah. Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, narrated to us Abu Kurayb, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Yusuf, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Jurayy ibn Samurah, he said: When there occurred between the people of Basrah what occurred between them and Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, I set out until I came to Madinah, and came to Maymunah bint al-Harith, and she is of Banu Hilal, and greeted her. She said: From where is the man? I said: From the people of Iraq. She said: From which people of Iraq? I said: From the people of Kufah. She said: From which people of Kufah? I said: From Banu Amir. She said: Welcome, nearness upon nearness, and spaciousness upon spaciousness; so what coming has brought you? I said: There occurred between Ali, and Talhah, and al-Zubayr what occurred, so I came and pledged allegiance to Ali. She said: So join him, for by Allah he was not misguided nor was anyone misguided through him, until she said it three times."
"21680","Abu Khalid al-Walibi from Maymunah. Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Waki, narrated to us al-Amash, from a shaykh I think he is Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"21681","Bilal ibn Yahya al-Absi from Maymunah. Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Musa, from Sad ibn Aws, from Bilal ibn Yahya, from Maymunah, she said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: What will you be when religion is confused, blood is shed, adornment appears, buildings are raised high, brothers differ, and the Ancient House is burned."
"21682","Abdullah al-Jazari from Maymunah. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar, narrated to us Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman, narrated to us Hassan ibn Ibrahim, from Mansur ibn Sad, from Abbad ibn Kathir, from Abdullah al-Jazari, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood between the row of men and the row of women, and said to the women: When you hear the adhan of this Abyssinian, say as he says."
"21683","Nudbah, freedwoman of Maymunah, from Maymunah. Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Nudbah, a freedwoman of Maymunah, she said: I entered upon Ibn Abbas, for Maymunah sent me to him, and there were two beds in his house. I returned to Maymunah and said: I see Ibn Abbas but keeping away from his family. Maymunah sent to Bint Mishrah al-Kindi, wife of Ibn Abbas, asking her. She said: There is no desertion between me and him, but I am menstruating. Maymunah sent to Ibn Abbas: Do you turn away from the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch one of his wives while menstruating, with a cloth upon her to the knee or to half the thigh. And Ibn Jurayj mentioned it from Ibn Shihab, from Habib freedman of Urwah, from Nudbah."
"21684","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Husayn ibn Numayr, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Husayn, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from a freedwoman of Maymunah bint al-Harith, she said: Maymunah sent me to Ibn Abbas, and I saw his bed set apart from his wife's bed, and with him that day was Bint Mishrah. She said: What is wrong with you? She said: This is what he does with me when I menstruate. She said: So I came to Maymunah and informed her. He said: And she said: So she sent me to him: What is this that you do? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch one of us while she was menstruating, with nothing upon her but her waist wrapper reaching half her thigh."
"21685","Narrated to us al-Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Salih, al-Layth narrated to me. Ha. And narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us Shuayb ibn Yahya, al-Layth informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Habib freedman of Urwah, from Nudbah freedwoman of Maymunah, from Maymunah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch one of his wives while she was menstruating, when upon her was a waist wrapper reaching half the thighs or the knees, wrapping herself with it."
"21686","Narrated to us Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti, narrated to us Wahb ibn Baqiyyah, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Habib freedman of Urwah, from a freedwoman of Maymunah, from Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch one of his wives while she was menstruating, when upon her was a waist wrapper reaching half the thighs or the knees."
"21687","Narrated to us Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Salih, narrated to us Anbasah ibn Khalid, narrated to us Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Habib freedman of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, that Nudbah, freedwoman of Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saw that his bed was set apart from his wife's bed, Bint Mishrah, so she returned to Maymunah and informed her of the return of her message, then said: And I saw her bed set apart from his bed, so I think there is desertion between them. Maymunah said to them: Return to Bint Mishrah, wife of Ibn Abbas, and ask her about that. I returned and asked her. She said: There is no desertion between us, but when I menstruate he sets his bed apart from my bed. Maymunah sent to Abdullah and was angry with him and said: O Abdullah, do you turn away from the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? By Allah, if one of his wives wrapped herself with a garment not reaching half her thighs, then he touched her body."
"21688","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Sad, my uncle narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, from Habib al-Araj freedman of Urwah, that Nudbah, freedwoman of Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him, that Maymunah sent her to Abdullah ibn Abbas - and he is the son of her sister. She said: So I came to him and found he had set his bed apart from his wife's bed, Bint Mishrah. She said: Where is he? Is he angry with his wife? It was said: No, but when she menstruates he keeps away from her. She said: So I returned to Maymunah and informed her how I found him. She said: Call him to me. I called him to her, and she said to him: Do you turn away from what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do? By Allah, he used to touch one of his wives when upon her was a waist wrapper reaching half the thighs or the knees."
"21689","Umm Manbudh al-Makkiyyah from Maymunah. Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Manbudh informed me, that his mother informed him, that while she was sitting with Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Ibn Abbas entered upon her and she said: Why do I see you disheveled? He said: Umm Ammar, my hairdresser, menstruated. She said: O son, what has menstruation to do with the hand? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to enter upon one of us while she was reclining menstruating, knowing that, and recline upon her and recite the Quran while reclining upon her, and enter upon her while she was standing menstruating and recline in her lap and recite the Quran, and she would stand while menstruating and spread for him the khumrah in his prayer place and he would pray upon it. O son, what has menstruation to do with the hand?"
"21690","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, narrated to us Sufyan, Manbudh al-Makki narrated to me, from his mother, she said: I was with Maymunah and Ibn Abbas entered upon her. She said: O son, why do I see you disheveled in head? He said: My hairdresser Umm Ammar is menstruating. She said: O son, what has menstruation to do with the hand? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to place his head in the lap of one of us while she was menstruating and pray upon it. O son, where is menstruation from the hand?"
"21691","al-Aliyah bint Subay from Maymunah. Narrated to us al-Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, Abdallah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Kathir ibn Farqad, from Abdullah ibn Malik ibn Hudhafah, from his mother al-Aliyah bint Subay, that Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to her that men of Quraysh passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dragging a sheep of theirs like a donkey. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: If you took its hide? They said: It is carrion. He said: Water and qaraz purify it."
"21692","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Sufyan, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee, so he said: Throw it and what is around it away and eat it."
"21693","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah, narrated to us Salamah ibn Shabib, narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar ibn Budhawayh informed us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse falling into ghee, so he said: If it is solid, throw it and what is around it away; and if it is liquid, do not approach it."
"21694","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee, the like of it."
"21695","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah, narrated to us Bakr ibn Abd al-Wahhab, Ikrimah ibn Jafar narrated to me, from Uqbah ibn Kathir, from Khirash, from Ibn Abdullah, from Maymunah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood between the row of men and women and said: O assembly of women, when you hear the adhan of this Abyssinian and his iqamah, say as he says, for you have for every letter a million million degrees. Umar said: This is for women, so what is for men? He said: Twofold, O Umar. Then he turned to the women and said: There is no woman who obeys and fulfills her husband's right, and remembers his goodness and does not betray him in herself or his wealth, but there will be between her and the martyrs one degree in Paradise; if her husband is a believing man of good character, she is his wife in Paradise, otherwise Allah will marry her to the martyrs."
"21696","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a sheep belonging to a freedwoman of Maymunah that she had been given from charity, dead, and said: Why did they not take its hide and tan it and benefit from it? They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is carrion. He said: Only eating it was forbidden."
"21697","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Yahya ibn Main, narrated to us Hajjaj, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, he said: Ata informed me, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Maymunah informed me, that a sheep died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not tan its hide and use it?"
"21698","Narrated to us al-Asfati, narrated to us Abu Yala al-Thawri, narrated to us Abu Safwan, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of dogs."
"21699","Narrated to us al-Asfati, narrated to us Abu al-Walid, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Kathir, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day listless, so I said: Why do I see you listless? He said: Jibril promised me and never broke his promise to me. He remained his day like that and his night, and in the house was a dog under a table of ours, so it was taken out and he took water in his hand and wiped its place with it. Then Jibril came and said: We do not enter a house in which there is an image or a dog. And he was spoken to about the dog of the small walled garden but he did not permit it."
"21700","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr, narrated to us Sufyan, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: I used to wash, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel."
"21701","Narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Imran, narrated to us Yahya ibn Khalaf, narrated to us Abu Dawud, narrated to us Sharik, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing makes water impure."
"21702","Narrated to us Ubayd, narrated to us Abu Bakr, narrated to us Waki, narrated to us al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from his maternal aunt Maymunah, she said: I put ghusl water for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he washed from janabah; he tilted the vessel with his left onto his right and washed his palms, then poured over his private part and washed it, then rubbed his hand on the ground, then rinsed his mouth and nose and washed his face and forearms, then poured over his head, then poured water over the rest of his body, then moved aside and washed his feet. She said: So I brought him a garment and he threw it away, and he began saying with the water like this, shaking off the water."
"21703","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari, narrated to us Ismah ibn Sulayman al-Khazzaz, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, she said: I washed from janabah, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and washed with my leftover. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have washed from it. He said: Water has no janabah upon it."
"21704","Narrated to us Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah, narrated to us Abu Ghassan, narrated to us Sharik, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Nothing makes water impure."
"21705","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Idris, from al-Amash, from Salim, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a towel and did not touch it, and he began saying with the water like this, meaning shaking it off."
"21706","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuyi and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, they said: narrated to us Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi, narrated to us al-Mubarak Abu Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Mutayyab narrated to us, that Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali went out in a funeral, and when it was placed on the bier he turned to the people and said: Straighten your rows and make your intercession good. Then Abu al-Malih said: Abdullah ibn Salit narrated to me - and he was the brother of Maymunah, Mother of the Believers - from Maymunah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever a community prays over, they are made intercessors for their brother. And a community is forty to a hundred, and a company is ten to forty, and a group is three to ten."
"21707","Narrated to us al-Judhuyi, narrated to us Uqbah ibn Mukram, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sisters are believers, meaning Maymunah bint al-Harith, and Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, and Salma wife of Hamzah, and Asma bint Umays."
"21708","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Humayd, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, that they disputed about the fasting of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Arafah. Maymunah said: I will send to him dates for you; if he is breaking fast he will not leave it. So she sent to him a cup of milk and he drank it while the people were looking."
"21709","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan, from Abi Bakkar al-Hakam ibn Farrukh, he said: I prayed with Abu al-Malih over a funeral and he said: Straighten your rows and let your intercession be good, and if I were to choose a man I would choose him. Abdullah ibn Abi al-Salil narrated to us, from one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Maymunah, and he was her foster brother, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim man over whom a community prays but they are made intercessors for him. Abu al-Malih said: A community is forty to a hundred."
"21710","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Sufyan al-Raqqi, narrated to us Ali ibn Maymun, narrated to us Khalid ibn Hayyan, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymunah - and Yazid was an orphan in her care - so he mentioned that a siwak kept in a vessel; if work or prayer busied her, otherwise she took the siwak and cleaned her teeth."
"21711","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Maymunah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me at Sarif while we were both lawful."
"21712","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Abi Fazarah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, he said: Maymunah narrated to me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her while he was lawful, and she was my maternal aunt."
"21713","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, and from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while he was lawful."
"21714","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Qazzaz, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Idris, narrated to us Marwan ibn Muawiyah, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Asamm, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymunah, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat he settled on his left thigh."
"21715","Narrated to us Ubayd, narrated to us Abu Bakr, narrated to us Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymunah, she said: A lizard was gifted to us and I prepared it. Two men of my people of Quraysh entered and I presented it to them as a gift. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered while they were eating, so he put his hand, then raised it and said: What is this? I said: A lizard gifted to us and I prepared it, so he threw it away. They went to throw what was in their hands, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Eat; you, people of Najd, eat it, and we, people of Tihamah, find it distasteful."
"21716","Narrated to us Ubayd, narrated to us Abu Bakr, narrated to us Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, he said: Maymunah narrated to me: When one of us menstruated and stood and wanted to return, he ordered her to wrap herself, then he touched her."
"21717","Narrated to us Ubayd, narrated to us Abu Bakr, narrated to us Ali ibn Mushir, from al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, he said: Maymunah narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"21718","Narrated to us Ubayd, narrated to us Abu Bakr, narrated to us Abbad ibn al-Awwam, narrated to us al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, he said: Maymunah narrated to me, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while I was opposite him, and sometimes his garment touched me when he prostrated."
"21719","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hisham, narrated to us Ali ibn al-Madini, narrated to us Sufyan, from Abi Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a khamisah, part of it upon her while she was menstruating."
"21720","Narrated to us Ubayd, narrated to us Abu Bakr, narrated to us Abbad ibn al-Awwam, narrated to us al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, he said: Maymunah narrated to me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on the khumrah."
"21721","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani, narrated to us Abu Shihab, from Abi Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Maymunah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in his mosque on his khumrah; his hands touched me while I was sleeping beside him and I was menstruating."
"21722","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, from Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: My ummah will remain in good with its affair held together so long as children of zina do not appear among them; when they appear I fear Allah will envelop them with punishment."
"21723","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Yala ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I freed a slave girl of mine, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and I informed him of freeing her. He said: May Allah reward you; had you given her to your maternal uncles it would have been greater for your reward."
"21724","Narrated to us al-Muttalib ibn Shuayb, narrated to us Abu Salih, al-Layth narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Kurayb, that Maymunah bint al-Harith informed him, that she freed a slave girl of hers, and he mentioned the like of it."
"21725","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Bakr ibn Khalaf, narrated to us Abd al-Wahhab, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is sweet and green."
"21726","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman, narrated to us Said ibn Abi Maryam, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Kurayb, from Maymunah, that the people doubted about the fasting of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafah, so Maymunah sent to him a milk bowl while he was standing at the standing place, and he drank from it while the people were looking."
"21727","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Salih, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, from his father, from Kurayb, he said: I heard Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lie with me while I was menstruating, with a garment between me and him."
"21728","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Kurayb ibn Abi Shaybah, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ziyad ibn Amr ibn Hind, from Ibn Hudhayfah, from Umm al-Muminin Maymunah, that she used to take debts. One of her family said to her: Do not do so, and disapproved of that to her. She said: Yes indeed, I heard my Prophet and my beloved (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no Muslim who takes a debt wanting to repay it but Allah will repay it for him in this world."
"21729","Narrated to us Ubayd, narrated to us Abu Bakr, narrated to us Sufyan, from Manbudh, from his mother, she said: Ibn Abbas entered upon Maymunah, the hadith."
"21730","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli, narrated to us Ali ibn al-Madini, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad, my father narrated to me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, from Habib al-Awar freedman of Urwah, that Nudbah, freedwoman of Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him, that Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sent her to Ibn Abbas, and he is the son of her sister. She said: So I came and found his bed moved away from his wife's bed, Bint Mishrah. I said: Where is he? Is he angry with his wife? They said: No, but when she menstruates he keeps away from her. I returned to Maymunah and informed her how I found him. She said: Call him to me. I called him, and she said to him: Do you turn away from what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do? By Allah, he used to touch one of his wives when upon her were garments reaching half the thighs or the knees."
"21731","Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba, narrated to us Abu Marwan al-Umani, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Ata ibn Yasar, from the Hilaliyyah who was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she had a black servant girl, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to free her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why do you not help with her the sons of your brother in herding sheep."
"21732","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, Ghundar narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, he said: I asked him: I pray witr with three? Then I go out to prayer fearing it will escape me. He said: It is not proper except with five or seven. So I asked him from whom? He said: From the trustworthy one, from Maymunah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21733","Narrated to us Ubayd, narrated to us Abu Bakr, narrated to us Waki, from al-Amash, he said: I think Abu Khalid al-Walibi mentioned it, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine."
"21734","Narrated to us Ubayd, narrated to us Abu Bakr, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi, from Sad ibn Aws, from Bilal ibn Yahya al-Absi, from Maymunah, she said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us one day: How will you be when religion is confused, subjects appear, reports differ, and the Ancient House is burned."
"21735","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal, narrated to us Yaqub ibn Humayd, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad and Hatim ibn Ismail, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her when she freed her servant: Had you ransomed your family with her from herding sheep it would have been better."
"21736","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati, narrated to us Said ibn Sulayman, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam. Ha. And narrated to us Mahmud ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh, narrated to us Salih ibn Umayr, from Hanzalah al-Sadusi, that he heard Abdullah ibn al-Harith saying: Maymunah narrated to me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rakahs before Asr."
"21737","Narrated to us Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh, narrated to us Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Iskandarani, narrated to us Abu Shurayh, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah, from Kurayb, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder at her house then prayed and did not perform wudu."
"21738","Narrated to us Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas, my father narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, that he heard Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, saying: I heard Maymunah saying: I freed my slave girl in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Had you given her to your maternal uncles it would have been greater for your reward."
"21739","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah, my father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ubaydullah ibn Utbah, he said: Maymunah took a debt of eight hundred dirhams, so her family said to her: Do you borrow when you have nothing to repay? She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever takes a debt while telling himself to repay it, Allah will help him with it."
"21740","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli, narrated to us Ali ibn al-Madini, narrated to us Wahb ibn Jarir, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Amash narrating from Husayn, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, that Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), borrowed three hundred dirhams. It was said to her: O Mother of the Believers, do you borrow when you have nothing? She said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever takes a debt wanting to repay it, Allah will help him with it."
"21741","Narrated to us Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh, narrated to us Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah, from Kurayb, that he heard Maymunah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder then prayed and did not perform wudu."
"21742","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj, narrated to us Said ibn Yahya al-Umawi, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) read Ha Mim, Ayn Sin Qaf and said: O Maymunah, do you read Ha Mim, Ayn Sin Qaf? I have been made to forget what is between its beginning and its end. So I read it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) read it."
"21743","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Irq al-Himsi, narrated to us Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak, narrated to us Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Nafi ibn Amir, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, that Maymunah was shrouded in a saffron-dyed shirt."
"21744","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and said: Is there any food? I said: No, except a bone given to a freedwoman of ours from charity. He said: Bring it, for it has reached its place."
"21745","Sawdah bint Zamah, may Allah be pleased with her. Narrated to us Abu Usamah Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah al-Halabi, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani al-Rusafi, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, he said: Sawdah bint Zamah ibn Qays ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Wudd ibn Nasr ibn Malik ibn Hisl ibn Amir ibn Luayy ibn Ghalib ibn Fihr, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her after Khadijah bint Khuwaylid in Makkah."
"21746","Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Mahdi al-Ikhmimi al-Misri, my uncle Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hanif, from his father, he said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Sawdah bint Zamah, and before him she was under al-Sakran ibn Amr, brother of Banu Amir ibn Luayy."
"21747","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj, narrated to us Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Aishah, she said: When Khadijah died, Khawlah bint Hakim ibn al-Awqas, wife of Uthman ibn Mazun, said, and that was in Makkah: O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry? He said: Whom? She said: If you wish a virgin and if you wish a previously married woman. He said: And who is the previously married woman? She said: Sawdah bint Zamah; she has believed in you and followed you upon what you are upon. He said: Go and mention me to her. So I went out and entered upon Sawdah and said: O Sawdah, what goodness and blessing has Allah brought upon you? She said: And what is that? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to propose you to him. She said: I would love to; enter upon my father and mention that to him. She said: And he is a very old shaykh who had stayed behind from Hajj. So I entered upon him and greeted him with the greeting of Jahiliyyah, then said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib sent me to propose Sawdah to him. He said: A noble match; so what does your companion say? She said: She loves that. He said: Call her to me. I called her, and he said: O Sawdah, this one says that Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib proposes to you and he is a noble match; do you love that I marry him to you? She said: Yes. He said: Call him to me. I called him and he came and he married her. Then her brother Abdullah ibn Zamah came from Hajj and began throwing dust on his head. He said after he became Muslim: I was foolish on the day I threw dust on my head that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Sawdah bint Zamah."
"21748","Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratis, narrated to us Said ibn Abi Maryam, Ha. And narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Rabi ibn Shahin, narrated to us Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, Ha. And narrated to us Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, narrated to us Abu Bilal al-Ashari, they said: narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not prefer any of us over another in apportioning, and hardly a day passed but he visited us all and drew near to each of us without touching, until he ended at the one whose day it was and spent the night with her. Sawdah bint Zamah had despaired and he wanted to separate from her, so she said: My day from you and my share is for Aishah, so he accepted that from her. About her was revealed: And if a woman fears cruelty or desertion from her husband, there is no sin upon them if they make terms of peace between them."
"21749","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, they said: narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that Sawdah gave her day to Aishah, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not want what women want."
"21750","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that Sawdah gifted her day to Aishah, so he apportioned to Aishah by her day and the day of Sawdah."
"21751","84 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: When Sawdah bint Zam'ah grew old, she gave her day to Aishah, and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - used to assign to Aishah the day of Sawdah."
"21752","85 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Sawdah feared that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would divorce her, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, keep me and do not divorce me, and give my day to Aishah. So Allah, Exalted and Majestic, sent down: {There is no sin upon them if they make terms of settlement between them, and settlement is best}. So whatever the two of them agree upon of anything, it is permissible."
"21753","86 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, he said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - intended to separate from Sawdah, so he called Abu Bakr and Umar to witness her divorce. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I have no desire for this world except to be gathered on the Day of Resurrection among your wives, so that I may have of the reward what they have."
"21754","87 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abu Hanifah, from al-Haytham, or Abu al-Haytham - Abu Bakr was in doubt - that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - divorced Sawdah with one divorce. So she sat in his path, and when he passed, she asked him to take her back and that she would give her share from him to whichever of his wives he wished, hoping to be raised on the Day of Resurrection as his wife. So he took her back and accepted that."
"21755","88 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Sawdah was a large-bodied woman whose body startled people."
"21756","What Sawdah bint Zam'ah narrated. 89 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Musa narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Salih, the freed slave of al-Taw'amah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Sawdah and Zaynab said: No camel shall ever move us after what we heard from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - meaning his saying: This, then the backs of mats. He said: So his wives used to perform Hajj except those two."
"21757","90 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban informed me, from Sawdah bint Zam'ah, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when he goes out, Uthman ibn Maz'un leads us in prayer until he comes to us. So the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to her: If you knew the knowledge of death, O daughter of Zam'ah, you would know that it is more severe than you reckon."
"21758","91 - al-Asfati narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ayyash, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Sawdah bint Zam'ah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: People will be raised barefoot, naked, uncircumcised, with sweat bridling them and reaching the lobes of the ears. So I said: Will some of us see others? He said: People will be preoccupied - {For every man among them that Day will have a matter to occupy him}."
"21759","92 - Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd ibn Zurarah, he said: The captives of Badr were brought, while Sawdah bint Zam'ah was with the family of Afra in their encampment over Awf and Mu'awwidh, the two sons of Afra - and that was before the veil was imposed upon them. She said: It was said that the captives of Badr had been brought, so I went to my house, and there I was before Suhayl ibn Amr, with his hands bound to his neck in a corner of the room. When I saw him, I could not control myself, and I said: Abu Yazid, you surrendered what was in your hands - would that you had died nobly? She said: By Allah, nothing startled me except the words of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - from inside the house: Against Allah and against His Messenger? So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I could not control myself when I saw Abu Yazid but that I said what I said."
"21760","93 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Amr al-Waki'i narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Sawdah bint Zam'ah, that she gave her day to Aishah."
"21761","94 - Wathilah ibn al-Hasan al-Irqi narrated to us, Kathir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Qays, he said: I heard Hudhayl ibn Shurahbil narrating, from one of the wives of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - that she had a dead sheep - the hadith."
"21762","What Ibn Abbas narrated from Sawdah. 95 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ghalib ibn Qa'id narrated to us, from Sharik, from Jabir, from Amir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Sawdah bint Zam'ah, she said: We had a sheep that died, so we threw it away. Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came and said: Why did you not make use of its hide? So we sent for it and skinned it, then tanned it and made it a waterskin, and we drank from it until it became worn out."
"21763","96 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Khalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, Ikrimah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, that a sheep belonging to Sawdah died. She said: So we tanned its skin and we used to make nabidh in it until it became a worn-out old skin."
"21764","97 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Manfa' ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Abu Isma'il al-Mu'addib narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Sawdah, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - she said: We had a sheep that died, so we tanned its skin, and we kept making nabidh in it until it became worn out."
"21765","98 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Sawdah, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - passed by a dead sheep and said: Why did you not enjoy the use of its hide?"
"21766","99 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Sawdah bint Zam'ah, she said: We had a sheep that died, so we threw it away. Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came and said: What happened to your sheep? We said: It died, so we threw it away. He said: Why did you not make use of its hide? I said: It is dead meat. So he recited this verse: {Say: I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to one who eats it except that it be dead meat} - only eating it has been forbidden to you. So they sent for its hide and tanned it, and they used it until it became a worn-out skin with them."
"21767","100 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Sawdah bint Zam'ah, that a sheep of theirs died, so the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Why did you not take its skin and tan it and make use of it?"
"21768","What Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated from Sawdah. 101 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi narrated to us, Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Yusuf ibn al-Zubayr, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from Sawdah, Mother of the Believers, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is a very old man who cannot perform Hajj - shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? So the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Tell me, if your father had a debt and you paid it, would it suffice for him? He said: Yes. He said: Perform Hajj on his behalf."
"21769","Zaynab bint Jahsh ibn Ribab al-Asadiyyah, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - may Allah be pleased with her. 102 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Among those who emigrated from Banu Asad, of their women: Zaynab bint Jahsh and other women - and he mentioned them."
"21770","An account of the marriage of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - to Zaynab, and of her age, her death, and reports about her. 103 - al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Mahdi al-Ikhmimi al-Misri narrated to us, my uncle Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, he said: Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - married Zaynab bint Jahsh, and before him she had been under Zayd ibn Harithah."
"21771","104 - Abu Usamah Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani' al-Rusafi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, he said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - married Zaynab bint Jahsh ibn Ri'ab ibn Asad ibn Khuzaymah, and her mother was Umaymah bint Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim, the paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: And she was the first of the wives of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - to die."
"21772","105 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ziyad al-Bakka'i narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Zaynab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - died in the year twenty."
"21773","106 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mundhir, he said: Zaynab bint Jahsh died during the caliphate of Umar - may Allah be pleased with them both."
"21774","107 - Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Isa ibn Tahman narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: Zaynab bint Jahsh used to boast over the wives of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: Your fathers married you off, while Allah married me from above the heaven."
"21775","108 - Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, he said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered his house with Umar ibn al-Khattab with him, and there was Zaynab bint Jahsh praying, supplicating in her prayer. So the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: She is indeed oft-sighing in devotion."
"21776","109 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn A'yan al-Harrani narrated to us, Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Kumayt ibn Zayd al-Asadi, he said: Madhkur, the freed slave of Zaynab bint Jahsh, narrated to me, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, she said: Several men of Quraysh proposed to me, so I sent my sister Hamnah to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - to consult him. So the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to her: Where is she from one who would teach her the Book of her Lord and the Sunnah of her Prophet? She said: And who is he, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Zayd ibn Harithah? He said: So Hamnah became intensely angry and said: O Messenger of Allah, would you marry the daughter of your paternal aunt to your freed slave? She said: She came to me and informed me, so I became angrier than her anger and said worse than her words. So Allah sent down: {It is not for a believing man or a believing woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decreed a matter, that they should have any choice in their affair}. She said: So I sent to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: I seek Allah's forgiveness and I obey Allah and His Messenger; do what you see fit. So he married me to Zayd, and I used to pity him. Then he complained of me to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - reproached me. Then I returned and attacked him with my tongue, so he complained of me to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: {Keep your wife to yourself and fear Allah}. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I shall divorce her. She said: So he divorced me. When my waiting period ended, I knew nothing except that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - had entered upon me in my house while my hair was uncovered. So I said: It is a decree from heaven. I said: O Messenger of Allah, without proposal or witnesses? He said: Allah is the One who marries, and Jibril is the witness."
"21777","110 - al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, he said: When the waiting period of Zaynab ended, the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to Zayd: Mention her to me. Zayd said: So I set out and said: O Zaynab, rejoice; the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - has sent to mention you. She said: I shall do nothing until I consult my Lord. So she stood toward her place of prayer, then the Qur'an came down, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came and entered upon her without permission."
"21778","111 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: Had the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - concealed anything of the revelation, he would have concealed this verse: {And you conceal within yourself what Allah will disclose, and you fear the people while Allah is more worthy that you fear Him. Then when Zayd had fulfilled his need from her, We married her to you}."
"21779","112 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: Had the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - concealed anything of the Book of Allah, he would have concealed this verse: {And when you say to the one upon whom Allah bestowed favor and you bestowed favor} up to His saying: {When Zayd had fulfilled his need, We married her to you}."
"21780","113 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, regarding His saying: {And when you say to the one upon whom Allah bestowed favor and you bestowed favor} - he said: Allah bestowed upon him Islam, and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - bestowed upon him freedom - {Keep your wife to yourself}. Qatadah said: Zayd came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: Zaynab's tongue is harsh upon me, and I wish to divorce her. So the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Fear Allah and keep your wife to yourself. And the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - loved that he divorce her, but he feared the people's talk if he commanded him to divorce her. So He sent down: {And you conceal within yourself what Allah will disclose, and you fear the people while Allah is more worthy that you fear Him. Then when Zayd had fulfilled his need from her} - he said: when Zayd divorced her - {We married her to you}."
"21781","114 - Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Salih al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, regarding His saying: {And when you say to the one upon whom Allah bestowed favor and you bestowed favor} - and he is Zayd ibn Harithah - {Allah bestowed favor upon him} with Islam, {and you bestowed favor upon him} - the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - freed him - {Keep your wife to yourself and fear Allah, and you conceal within yourself what Allah will disclose, and you fear the people}. He said: He concealed within himself the wish that he would divorce her. He said: al-Hasan said: No verse was sent down upon him more severe than His saying: {And you conceal within yourself}. Had the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - concealed anything of the revelation, he would have concealed it: {And you fear the people while Allah is more worthy that you fear Him}. He said: The Prophet of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - feared the people's talk. {Then when Zayd had fulfilled his need from her} - when Zayd divorced her - {We married her to you}: Zaynab bint Jahsh used to boast over the wives of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: As for you, your fathers married you off, while as for me, the Lord of the Throne married me. {And fear Allah} - he said: He kept saying: O Prophet of Allah, her character has become harsh upon me, and I shall divorce this woman. Whenever Zayd said that, the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would say: {Keep your wife to yourself and fear Allah}."
"21782","115 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, regarding His saying: {And when you say to the one upon whom Allah bestowed favor} with Islam, {and you bestowed favor upon him} - that you freed him - {Keep your wife to yourself} - and he is Zayd ibn Harithah."
"21783","116 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: There was revealed concerning Zaynab bint Jahsh: {And you conceal within yourself what Allah will disclose}."
"21784","117 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, regarding His saying: {And you conceal within yourself what Allah will disclose} - in the soul of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was his love that he divorce her and that he marry her; but Allah refused except to inform of what the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - had concealed within himself."
"21785","118 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, and al-Hawd narrated to us, and Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us, Musaddad and Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us - they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - give a wedding feast for any of his wives like what he gave for Zaynab, for he slaughtered a sheep."
"21786","119 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, regarding His saying: {The established way of Allah among those who passed before} - he said: Dawud and the woman he married, whose husband's name was al-Yasa' - so that is a precedent regarding Muhammad and Zaynab."
"21787","120 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, regarding His saying: {And the command of Allah is a decree determined} - likewise from His way regarding Dawud and the woman, and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and Zaynab."
"21788","121 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athmah narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Munayyib, from Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathamah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came to the house of Zayd ibn Harithah and sought permission. Zaynab gave him permission while she had no head-cover on her, so she cast the sleeve of her shift over her head. He asked her about Zayd, and she said: He went out a short while ago, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - rose, with a murmur on his lips. Zaynab said: So I followed him and heard him saying: Blessed is the Turner of hearts. He kept saying it until he disappeared from sight."
"21789","122 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Asad al-Bajali narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, from al-Mu'alla ibn Irfan, from Muhammad ibn Jahsh, he said: Aishah and Zaynab boasted against one another. Zaynab said: I am the one whom Allah married from the heaven. And Aishah said: I am the one whose exoneration came down when Safwan ibn al-Mu'attal carried me. Zaynab said to her: What did you say when you mounted? She said: I said: Allah suffices me, and He is the best Disposer of affairs. She said: You spoke the word of the believers."
"21790","123 - Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Salih al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, regarding His saying: {It is not for a believing man or a believing woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decreed a matter, that they should have any choice in their affair; and whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger has certainly strayed into clear error} - he said: This verse came down concerning Zaynab bint Jahsh, and she was the daughter of the paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - proposed to her, so she was pleased, thinking he was proposing her for himself. When she learned that he was proposing her for Zayd ibn Harithah, she refused and objected. So Allah sent down: {It is not for a believing man or a believing woman} - the verse."
"21791","124 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - proposed to Zaynab, and she was the daughter of his paternal aunt, intending her for Zayd. She thought he intended her for himself, and when she learned that he intended her for Zayd, she refused. So Allah sent down: {It is not for a believing man or a believing woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decreed a matter, that they should have any choice in their affair}. So she was pleased and submitted."
"21792","An account of the revelation of the verse of the veil at the marriage of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - to Zaynab. 125 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Ja'd Abu Uthman, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - consummated marriage with one of his wives - meaning Zaynab - so Umm Sulaym made hays, then put it in a stone vessel, while they that day were in severe hardship. She said: Take this to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and convey my greeting to him, and tell him that this is a small portion from us. So I came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: O Messenger of Allah, Umm Sulaym sent this to you, conveying her greeting to you, and saying to you: O Messenger of Allah, this from us to you is small. He looked at it and said: Put it down. So I put it in a corner of the house. Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to me: Go and invite so-and-so and so-and-so and so-and-so - and he named many men - and whomever you meet of the Muslims. So I invited those he named for me and whomever I met of the Muslims. I came back with the house full, and the bench and the room - so we asked Anas: How many were they? He said: About three hundred - so the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - called me with the stone vessel. I brought it, and he placed his hand upon it and mentioned Allah's name and supplicated. Then he said: Let them sit in circles of ten by ten, and let each person eat from what is in front of him. So they sat in circles of ten by ten, mentioned Allah's name and ate, and rose; whenever a group finished, they stood and others followed them, until all of them had eaten. Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to me: Lift it. I do not know whether it was fuller when I put it down or when I lifted it. Groups of people remained in the house of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - conversing, and they lengthened the talk, weighing heavily upon the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was the most modest of people, yet they did not realize that they were weighing heavily upon the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and that was hard upon them. So the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - stood and left them. When they saw the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - return, they thought they had weighed heavily upon him, so they hastened to the door and went out. Anas said: Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came, let down the curtain and entered, and stayed a little. Then the revelation came down upon him, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came out reciting: {O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet except when you are permitted} to the end of the verses. Anas said: So I am the people most recently acquainted with these verses; the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - recited them to me."
"21793","126 - Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinna'i narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Hudhali narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, he said: I said to Anas ibn Malik: Inform me of the most wondrous thing you saw of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: When the Prophet of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - married Zaynab bint Jahsh, my mother said to me: O Anas, the Prophet of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - has become a bridegroom, and I do not see that he has any midday meal. Bring that leather skin of clarified butter and dates amounting to a mudd. So she made hays for him and said: O Anas, take this to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and his wife. When I came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - with a stone vessel containing that hays, he said: Put it in a corner of the house, and go and invite for me Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, and a group of his companions, then invite for me the people of the mosque and whomever you see on the road. I kept marveling at the scantiness of the food and the multitude of those he commanded me to invite, but I disliked disobeying him until the house and the room were full. He said: O Anas, do you see anyone left? I said: No, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Bring that stone vessel. So I brought that stone vessel and placed it before him. He dipped three fingers into the vessel, and the vessel kept increasing and rising. They ate the midday meal and went out, until when all of them had finished, there remained in the vessel about what I had brought. He said: Place it before Zaynab. So I went out and covered her door with palm stalks. Thabit said: So we said: O Abu Hamzah, how many do you think ate from that vessel? He said: I reckon seventy-one or seventy-two."
"21794","127 - Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Isa ibn Tahman narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - gave a wedding feast for Zaynab bint Jahsh with bread and meat."
"21795","128 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I am the most knowledgeable of people concerning this verse. When Zaynab was presented to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - she was with him in the house, and he prepared food. Then people came, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - kept going out while the people stayed in their places, and returning while the people sat. So Allah sent down: {O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet except when you are permitted to a meal, without awaiting its preparation. But when you are invited, then enter; and when you have eaten, then disperse, without seeking to remain for conversation. Indeed, that used to annoy the Prophet and he was shy of you, but Allah is not shy of the truth. And when you ask them for something, ask them from behind a partition}. So the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - drew the veil, and the people stood."
"21796","129 - Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Isa ibn Tahman narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The verse of the veil came down concerning Zaynab bint Jahsh."
"21797","130 - Abd Allah ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, that Anas ibn Malik said: I am the most knowledgeable of people concerning the veil; Ubayy ibn Ka'b used to ask me about it. Anas said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - became a bridegroom with Zaynab bint Jahsh, and he had married her in Madinah. He invited the people to food after midday. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - sat, and men sat with him after the people had risen, until the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - stood and walked, and I walked with him until he reached the door of Aishah's room. Then he thought they had gone out, so he returned, and I returned with him, and there they were still sitting. So he drew the curtain between me and him, and the verse of the veil came down."
"21798","131 - al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I was the most knowledgeable of people of the place of the veil when it was sent down - and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Salih ibn Kaysan."
"21799","132 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastawa'i narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saw a woman and she pleased him, so he entered upon Zaynab bint Jahsh and fulfilled his need from her. Then he went out and said: A woman comes in the image of a devil and turns away in the image of a devil. So whoever feels that, let him go to his wife, for that dispels what is in his soul."
"21800","133 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to his wives: The first of you to follow me will be the longest of you in hand. Aishah said: So when we gathered after the death of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - we used to stretch our hands along the wall, competing. We kept doing that until Zaynab bint Jahsh ibn Ri'ab died. She was a short woman and was not the tallest of us, so we knew that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - had meant by length of hand: charity. She was a skilled craftswoman who worked with her hands and gave it in charity in the path of Allah."
"21801","134 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Waki' and my father narrated to us - they said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, that he prayed with Umar over Zaynab, and she was the first of the wives of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - to die, and he used to like that whoever had seen her in her life should lower her into her grave. So he sent to the wives of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -: Who shall lower her into her grave? They said: Whoever used to see her in her life, let him lower her into her grave."
"21802","What Zaynab bint Jahsh narrated. Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan from Zaynab. 135 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon us saying: Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near; there has been opened today of the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj like this - and he circled his thumb and the one next to it. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we perish while the righteous are among us? He said: Yes, when filth increases. Abd al-Razzaq did not mention Umm Habibah in the chain from Ma'mar."
"21803","136 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me that Zaynab bint Abi Salamah was informed, from Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon her in fright, saying: Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near; there has been opened today of the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj like this - and he circled with his thumb and the one next to it. Zaynab said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we perish while the righteous are among us? He said: Yes, when filth increases."
"21804","137 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us - and we need no one else in it - Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Habibah bint Umm Habibah, from her mother Umm Habibah, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - woke from sleep with his face red, saying: There is no god but Allah; woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near; there has been opened today of the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj like this - and Sufyan made a ten with his fingers - I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we perish while the righteous are among us? He said: Yes, when filth increases. Sufyan said: I retain in this hadith four women from al-Zuhri, and they had seen the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -: two of his wives, Umm Habibah and Zaynab, and two of his stepdaughters: Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, and Habibah bint Umm Habibah, whose father Ubayd Allah ibn Jahsh died in the land of Abyssinia."
"21805","138 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Habibah, from Umm Habibah, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - woke from his sleep in fright and said: Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near; there has been opened today of the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj like this - and he circled with his two fingers, the thumb and the one next to it. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we perish while the righteous are among us? He said: Yes, when filth increases."
"21806","139 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, from his father, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, that she had a brass washbowl, and she said: I used to comb in it the head of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21807","Zaynab bint Umm Salamah from Zaynab bint Jahsh. 140 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, and al-Hawd, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, and al-Hawd, and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us - all of them from Malik, from Anas, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Humayd ibn Nafi', from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, she said: I entered upon Zaynab bint Jahsh when her brother died, so she called for perfume and touched some of it. Then she said: I have no need of perfume, but I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three days, except over a husband for four months and ten days."
"21808","Hidmir, the freed slave of Zaynab, from Zaynab. 141 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu al-Qasim, the freed slave of Zaynab, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was sleeping at her house while Husayn crawled about in the house. She was heedless of him, so he crawled until he reached the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and climbed upon his belly, then placed his private part in his navel. She said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - woke up, so I rose to him and lifted him off his belly. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Leave my son alone. When he had finished urinating, he took a jug of water and poured it over it. Then he said: Water is poured over the urine of a boy, and that of a girl is washed. She said: He performed ablution, then stood to pray and embraced him; when he bowed and prostrated, he put him down, and when he stood, he carried him. When he sat, he supplicated, raising his hands and saying - and when he had finished the prayer, I said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw you do today something I never saw you do. He said: Jibril came to me and informed me that my son will be killed. I said: Then show me. So he brought me red soil."
"21809","142 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Habibah, from Umm Habibah, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - woke from his sleep with his face red, saying: There is no god but Allah; woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near; there has been opened today of the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj like this - and he made a ten with his hand, meaning ten. Zaynab said: So I said: Shall we perish while the righteous are among us? He said: Yes, when filth increases."
"21810","143 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu al-Miqdam Thabit ibn Hurmuz, from Adi ibn Dinar, from Umm Qays bint Mihsan, she said: I entered upon Zaynab bint Jahsh with her face red, so I said: What is wrong with you? She said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon me while I was sleeping and struck me with a mijassah he had - I said: What is a mijassah? She said: A white palm frond - and said: By Allah, this is a time when great tribulations have descended. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we perish while the righteous are among us? He said: Yes; then those who feared Allah will be saved."
"21811","144 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, from his father, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, she said: We had a brass washbowl in which I used to comb the head of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21812","145 - Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hassan ibn Musa and Suwayd ibn Nasr narrated to us, and al-Hawd, and Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us - they said: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, she said: A woman asked the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: She suffers prolonged bleeding. He said: She sits out the days of her periods, then bathes and delays the noon prayer and hastens the afternoon prayer, and bathes and prays; and she delays the sunset prayer and hastens the night prayer and prays them both, and she bathes for the dawn prayer."
"21813","146 - Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Kulthum, from Zaynab, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - bequeathed to the women their house-plots."
"21814","147 - Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Idris, from Layth, from Hidmir, a freed slave of Banu Abs, from a freed slave of Zaynab bint Jahsh called Abu al-Qasim, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - took a midday nap in my house, when Husayn came - a boy - until he sat upon the belly of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - then placed his private part in his navel. She said: So I rose to him, and he said: Bring me water. So I brought him water and he poured it over it. Then he said: The urine of a girl is washed, and water is poured over that of a boy."
"21815","Zaynab bint Khuzaymah al-Hilaliyyah, and she is Umm al-Masakin. 148 - Abu Usamah Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani' al-Rusafi narrated to us, my grandfather Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - married Zaynab bint Khuzaymah, and she is Umm al-Masakin; she was named so for her abundant feeding of the poor. She is of Banu Hilal ibn Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah, and she died while the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was alive; she stayed with him only a short while."
"21816","149 - Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Damdam ibn Zur'ah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from the hadith of Habib ibn Ubayd, from the hadith of al-Abahh al-Sulami, that a woman of Banu Asad said: I was one day at Zaynab, the wife of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while we were preparing her with red ochre dye. While we were thus, the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon us; when he saw the red dye, he turned back. When Zaynab saw that, she knew that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - disliked what she had done, so she took water and washed her garments and concealed every redness. Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - returned and looked and saw nothing, so he entered."
"21817","150 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - married Zaynab bint Khuzaymah al-Hilaliyyah, Umm al-Masakin; before him she had been with al-Husayn, or with al-Tufayl ibn al-Harith. She died in Madinah, the first of his wives to die."
"21818","Juwayriyah bint al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar ibn al-Harith ibn A'idh ibn Malik ibn al-Mustaliq of Khuza'ah, and the name of al-Mustaliq is Khuzaymah. 151 - al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Mahdi al-Ikhmimi narrated to us, my uncle Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - took captive Juwayriyah bint al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar of Banu al-Mustaliq of Khuza'ah, in his expedition in which he destroyed Manat, the expedition of al-Muraysi'."
"21819","152 - Abu Usamah Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani' al-Rusafi narrated to us, my grandfather Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - took captive Juwayriyah bint al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar ibn A'idh ibn Malik ibn al-Mustaliq of Khuza'ah, and the name of al-Mustaliq is Khuzaymah, on the day he encountered Banu al-Mustaliq."
"21820","153 - Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Tustari narrated to us, Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah bint al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - died in the year fifty-six."
"21821","154 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Zakariyya, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Juwayriyah was the property of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - so he freed her and made her freeing her dowry, and every captive of Banu al-Mustaliq was freed."
"21822","155 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: Juwayriyah said to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -: Your wives boast over me and say: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - did not marry you. He said: Did I not magnify your dowry; did I not free forty of your people?"
"21823","156 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: I wrote to Nafi' asking him: Was the invitation before the fighting? He wrote to me that that was in the beginning of Islam, and that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - raided Banu al-Mustaliq while they were heedless, with their cattle being watered. He killed their fighters and took their captives captive, and Juwayriyah bint al-Harith was taken. Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to me this hadith, and he was that day in that army."
"21824","157 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ali ibn Bakkar narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - chose Juwayriyah for himself."
"21825","158 - Abu Shu'ayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah and Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hayyan each narrated to me - each narrated to me part of the hadith of Banu al-Mustaliq - he said: It reached the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - that Banu al-Mustaliq were gathering against him, and their leader was al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar, the father of Juwayriyah bint al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. When the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - heard of them, he went out to them until he met them at a water of theirs called al-Muraysi', toward Qudayd by the coast. The people crowded and fought, and Allah defeated Banu al-Mustaliq; al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar, the father of Juwayriyah, was killed, and those of them who were killed were killed. Allah granted His Messenger their children and women as spoils, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - took many captives from them and divided them among the Muslims. Among the women taken that day was Juwayriyah bint al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar, the chief lady of the women of her people."
"21826","159 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: Juwayriyah bint al-Harith ibn al-Mustaliq fell in the share of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas - or a cousin of his - so she contracted to buy her freedom. She came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - seeking his help in her contract. By Allah, no sooner did she appear at the door of the room than I disliked her; she was a beautiful woman whom no one saw but she captivated him. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I am Juwayriyah bint al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar, the chief of his people, and there has befallen me of calamity what you have seen. I have fallen in the share of Thabit ibn Qays - or a cousin of his - and I have contracted with him for myself. So I have come to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - seeking his help in his contract - and he mentioned the hadith in full."
"21827","What Juwayriyah narrated. Ibn Abbas from Juwayriyah. 160 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freed slave of the family of Talhah, he said: I heard Kurayb narrating from Ibn Abbas, from Juwayriyah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - passed by her early in the morning while she was in the mosque supplicating, then passed by her near midday and said: Are you still upon that? She said: Yes. He said: Shall I not teach you words that equal them - and necks, or their weight: Glory be to Allah as many as His creation, three times; Glory be to Allah to His own pleasure, three times; Glory be to Allah the weight of His Throne, three times; Glory be to Allah the ink of His words. Her name had been Barrah, so the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - named her Juwayriyah."
"21828","161 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and al-Hawd, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us - they said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freed slave of the family of Talhah, narrated to me, from Abu Rashdin, from Ibn Abbas, from Juwayriyah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - passed by her when he had prayed the dawn prayer - or after he prayed the dawn prayer - while she remembered Allah until the day rose, remaining so. He said: I have said since I left you three phrases that are greater and weightier - or heavier - than what you said: Glory be to Allah as many as His creation; Glory be to Allah to His own pleasure; Glory be to Allah the weight of His Throne; Glory be to Allah the ink of His words."
"21829","162 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freed slave of the family of Talhah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Juwayriyah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - went out from her early in the morning while she was in her mosque remembering Allah - and he mentioned the like of it."
"21830","163 - Muhammad ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Juwayriyah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - went out from her - and he mentioned the hadith."
"21831","Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq from Juwayriyah. 164 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, that Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq claimed that Juwayriyah, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - informed him, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon her and said: Is there any food? She said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah; I have no food except a bone of a sheep given to my freed slavewoman from charity. He said: Bring it near, for it has reached its lawful place."
"21832","165 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Numayr al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Uqayl, and Rashdin ibn Sa'd, from Uqayl, and Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Juwayriyah, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon her and said: Is there any food? She said: No, by Allah, except a bone of a sheep given to my freed slavewoman from charity. He said: Bring it near, for it has reached its lawful place."
"21833","166 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, he said: Juwayriyah bint al-Harith narrated to me, she said: We had a freed slavewoman to whom something was given in charity, so she cooked it. He said: Bring it near, for it has reached its lawful place - meaning the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21834","167 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Juwayriyah bint al-Harith, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon her and said: Do you have any food? She said: No, by Allah, except a bone of a sheep given to my freed slavewoman from charity. He said: Bring it near, for it has reached its lawful place."
"21835","168 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, and al-Hawd, and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Hawd, and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Madani narrated to us - they said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, that he heard Juwayriyah bint al-Harith saying: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon me and said: Is there any food? I said: No, except a bone given to our freed slavewoman from charity. He said: Bring it near, for it has reached its lawful place."
"21836","169 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my uncle narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, that Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq informed him, that Juwayriyah bint al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - informed him: That her freed slavewoman was given meat in charity, so she cooked it. When the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - returned, he said: Do you have any supper? I said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so was given a piece of meat in charity, and she has cooked it. So the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Bring it near, for it has reached its lawful place - and he ate from it."
"21837","al-Tufayl, the son of Juwayriyah's brother, from Juwayriyah. 170 - Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from his maternal aunt Umm Uthman, from al-Tufayl, the son of Juwayriyah's brother, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - he said: Whoever wears silk in this world, Allah will clothe him on the Day of Resurrection in a garment of fire, or a garment of His fire."
"21838","171 - Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from his maternal uncle Abu Uthman, from al-Tufayl, the son of Juwayriyah's brother, from Juwayriyah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever wears silk in this world, Allah will clothe him in a garment of fire."
"21839","172 - al-Husayn ibn Ghulayb narrated to us, Imran ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from the freed slave of Bakr ibn Sawadah, from a freed slave of Juwayriyah, from Juwayriyah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - used to dislike that food be eaten until the vehemence of its steam had gone."
"21840","Safiyyah bint Huyayy ibn Akhtab, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - from reports about her. 173 - Abu Usamah Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani' al-Rusafi narrated to us, my grandfather Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - took captive Safiyyah bint Huyayy ibn Akhtab of Banu al-Nadir on the day of Khaybar, while she was a bride of Kinanah ibn Abi al-Huqayq."
"21841","174 - al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Mahdi al-Ikhmimi al-Misri narrated to us, my uncle Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - took captive Safiyyah bint Huyayy of Banu al-Nadir, and she was of what Allah granted him as spoils."
"21842","175 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah - may Allah be pleased with her - she said: Safiyyah was of the select spoils."
"21843","176 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Bashir al-Shami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Waqid narrated to us, al-Nahhas ibn Qahm narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani, from Abu Barzah, he said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - encamped at Khaybar while Safiyyah was a bride in her bridal garments. She saw in a dream as though the sun had descended until it fell upon her breast, so she related that to her husband. He said: By Allah, you wish for nothing but this king who has come down upon us. Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - conquered it and struck her husband's neck in execution, and the youths of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - there presented themselves to marry her, until the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - cast dates for them upon a halved cloth and said: Eat the wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah for Safiyyah."
"21844","177 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: Safiyyah had greenness in her eyes, so the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to her: What is this greenness in your eyes? She said: I said to my husband: I saw in what the sleeper sees a moon falling into my lap, so he slapped me and said: Do you desire the kingdom of Yathrib? She said: And none was more hateful to me than the Messenger of Allah; he had killed my father and my husband. He kept apologizing to me, saying: O Safiyyah, your father incited the Arabs against me, and did and did - until that left my soul."
"21845","178 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - freed Safiyyah and made her freeing her dowry."
"21846","179 - al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda' al-Antaki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - freed Safiyyah and made her freeing her dowry."
"21847","180 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, and al-Hawd, and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, and al-Hawd, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us - they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - freed Safiyyah and made her freeing her dowry."
"21848","181 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - freed Safiyyah and made her freeing her dowry."
"21849","182 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - freed Safiyyah and made her freeing her dowry."
"21850","183 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Aslami, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, that Anas ibn Malik informed him, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - declared Safiyyah free of pregnancy by one menstruation."
"21851","184 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Wa'il ibn Dawud, from his father Bakr ibn Wa'il, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - gave a wedding feast for Safiyyah with sawiq and dates."
"21852","185 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, and al-Hawd, and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, and al-Hawd, and Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Saffar narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us - they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came to the people of Khaybar when the sun had risen - and he mentioned the hadith."
"21853","186 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: It reached Safiyyah that Hafsah said: The daughter of a Jew. She wept, so the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon her while she wept and said: What is wrong with you? She said: Hafsah said to me that I am the daughter of a Jew. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to her: You are the daughter of a prophet, and your uncle is indeed a prophet, and you are under a prophet - so in what does she boast over you? Then he said: Fear Allah, O Hafsah."
"21854","187 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Sumayyah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - found fault with Safiyyah over something, so Safiyyah said to me: Would you please reconcile the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - with me, and your day is mine? So I wore a head-cover of mine dyed with saffron, sprinkled it with water, then came and sat beside the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said to me: Away from me, for it is not your day. I said: That is the bounty of Allah; He gives it to whom He wills. I informed him of the report, and he was reconciled with her."
"21855","188 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Sumayyah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was on a journey, and the camel of Safiyyah fell ill, while Zaynab had extra mounts. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to her: The camel of Safiyyah has fallen ill - would you give her a camel? She said: Should I give that Jewess? So the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - became angry and boycotted her for the rest of Dhu al-Hijjah, and Muharram, and Safar, and days of Rabi', until she lifted her goods and her bed, thinking he had no need of her. While she was one day sitting at midday, she saw his shadow approaching, so she restored her bed and her goods."
"21856","What Safiyyah bint Huyayy narrated. What Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated from Safiyyah. 189 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Safiyyah bint Huyayy, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was in retreat, so I came to him at night in the mosque and spoke with him. Then I stood, and he stood with me to escort me back. Her dwelling was in the house of Usamah ibn Zayd. Two men of the Ansar passed by, and when they saw the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - they hastened. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Take your time; she is Safiyyah bint Huyayy. They said: Glory be to Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Satan runs through the son of Adam like blood, and I feared he might cast something into your hearts - or he said: evil."
"21857","190 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us - they said: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, he said: Safiyyah bint Huyayy, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - narrated to me, she said: I came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - speaking with him while he was in retreat in the mosque. He stood with me one of the nights to deliver me to my house. Two men of the Ansar met him, and when they saw him, they were shy and turned back. He said: Come forth; she is only Safiyyah, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. They said: Allah forbid; Glory be to Allah. He said: I do not say to you that you would think evil, but I know that Satan runs through man like blood."
"21858","191 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ali ibn Husayn, that Safiyyah bint Huyayy, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - informed him, that she came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - visiting him while he was in retreat in the mosque in the last ten of Ramadan. She spoke with him for a while, then stood to return, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - stood with her to escort her. When he emerged near the door of the mosque, at the door of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - two men of the Ansar passed by him; they greeted the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - then went on. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to them: Take your time; she is only Safiyyah bint Huyayy. They said: Glory be to Allah, O Messenger of Allah - and what the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said weighed heavily upon them. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Satan reaches of man the reach of blood, and I feared he might cast something into your hearts."
"21859","192 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati and Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us - they said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my brother narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Atiq, from Ibn Shihab, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Safiyyah - she informed him - that she came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - visiting him while he was in retreat in the mosque - and he mentioned the hadith."
"21860","193 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn al-Buhturi al-Ta'i al-Himsi narrated to us, Bishr ibn Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from his father, from al-Zuhri, he said: Ali ibn Husayn informed me that Safiyyah, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - informed him - and he mentioned the hadith."
"21861","Abd Allah ibn Safwan ibn Umayyah from Safiyyah. 194 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Shadh ibn al-Fayyad narrated to us, Hashim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Kinanah, from Safiyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - freed me and made my freeing my dowry."
"21862","195 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Shadh ibn al-Fayyad narrated to us, Hashim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Kinanah, from Safiyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon me with four thousand date-stones before me with which I glorified Allah. He said: O daughter of Huyayy, what is this? I said: I glorify Allah with them. He said: I have glorified since I stood over you with more than this. I said: Then teach me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Say: Glory be to Allah as many as what He created of things."
"21863","196 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Shadh ibn al-Fayyad narrated to us, Hashim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Kinanah, from Safiyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon me while I wept. He said: What makes you weep, O daughter of Huyayy? I said: I have heard that Aishah and Hafsah disparage me and say: We are better than her; we are the cousins of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and his wives. He said: Why did you not say: How can you be better than me, while my father is Harun, and my uncle is Musa, and my husband is Muhammad - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21864","Kinanah, the freed slave of Safiyyah, from Safiyyah. 197 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Umayyah ibn Safwan, from his grandfather, from Safiyyah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: This House will surely be faced by an army that raids it, until when they are in a desert land, the middle of them will be swallowed; the first of them will call to the last of them, and all of them will be swallowed. None of them will escape except the lone survivor who informs of them."
"21865","Muslim ibn Safwan from Safiyyah. 198 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Safwan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Idris al-Murhibi, from Muslim ibn Safwan, from Safiyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: People will not cease raiding this House until an army raids it; when they are in a desert land, the first of them and the last of them will be swallowed, and the middle of them will not escape. It was said: What if among them is one who dislikes it? He said: Allah will raise them according to what is in their souls."
"21866","Suhayrah bint Jayfar from Safiyyah. 199 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, and al-Hawd, and Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us - they said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Hakim, from Suhayrah bint Jayfar, she said: We went out as pilgrims and passed by Madinah, so we entered upon Safiyyah bint Huyayy and asked her about drinks. She said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - forbade nabidh of the earthen jar. Here ends the hadith of the wives of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - may Allah be pleased with them."
"21867","The chapter of alif: those named Asma. Asma bint Abi Bakr al-Siddiq - may Allah be pleased with her - and her mother was Qutaylah bint Abd al-Uzza ibn Abd As'ad of Banu Malik. An account of her age and death, and reports about her. 200 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Madini Fustuqah narrated to us, he said: Asma bint Abi Bakr al-Siddiq died in the year seventy-three, days after her son Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr. She was the sister of Aishah by her father, and the mother of Asma bint Abi Bakr was Qutaylah bint Abd al-Uzza ibn Abd As'ad, of Banu Malik ibn Hisl. Asma was one hundred years old the day she died; she was born twenty-seven years before the calendar, and seventeen years before the mission of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and Asma was born to Abu Bakr when he was twenty-one years old."
"21868","201 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la al-Taymi narrated to us, from his father Ya'la ibn Harmalah, he said: I entered Makkah after Ibn al-Zubayr had been killed, and his mother Asma bint Abi Bakr came - an old, aged, tall woman, blind - and said to al-Hajjaj: Is it not time for this rider to come down?"
"21869","What Asma bint Abi Bakr narrated. 202 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muslim al-Qurri, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the temporary Hajj and he permitted it, while Ibn al-Zubayr forbade it. Ibn Abbas said: This is the mother of Ibn al-Zubayr narrating: That the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - permitted it. So enter upon her and ask her. He said: So we entered upon her, and there was a bulky tall woman. She said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - permitted it."
"21870","What Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated from Asma: Hisham ibn Urwah from his father. 203 - Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: My mother came to me while she was a polytheist, during the treaty of Quraysh when they had made a treaty with the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and their term. So I sought a ruling from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come to me while she is desirous - shall I keep ties with her? He said: Yes, keep ties with your mother."
"21871","204 - Abu Arubah al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karimah Abu al-Mu'afa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: I heard Asma bint Abi Bakr saying: My mother came to me from Makkah to Madinah during the truce of Quraysh while she was a polytheist. I said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come to me while she is desirous - shall I keep ties with her? The Prophet of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to her: Keep ties with her."
"21872","205 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come to me while she is desirous and fearful - shall I keep ties with her? He said: Keep ties with her."
"21873","206 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - the like of it."
"21874","207 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah informed us, from Urwah, that Asma bint Abi Bakr said: My mother came to me while she was desirous and a polytheist. I said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come while she is desirous and a polytheist - shall I keep ties with her? The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Keep ties with her."
"21875","208 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, he said: My father informed me that he heard Asma bint Abi Bakr saying: My mother came to me while she was desirous, during the treaty of Quraysh. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I keep ties with her? He said: Yes."
"21876","209 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and al-Hawd, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us - they said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, and Fatimah bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I prepared a provision bag for the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - in the house of Abu Bakr when he intended to emigrate to Madinah. She said: We found nothing with which to tie his provision bag nor his waterskin, so I said to Abu Bakr: By Allah, I find nothing to tie with except my waist-wrapper. He said: Split it in two; tie the waterskin with one and the provision bag with the other. So I did, and for that I was named Dhat al-Nitaqayn."
"21877","210 - Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: Asma said: When I gave birth to Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he was brought to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and he rubbed him and named him Abd Allah. Then he came later, when he was seven years old - or eight - to pledge allegiance to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - al-Zubayr having commanded him to do that. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - smiled when he saw him coming and pledged him."
"21878","211 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Ghanim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Asma, she said: I ate horse meat in the time of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21879","212 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb al-Askari narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Sa'id al-Ayli narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We slaughtered a horse in the time of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and ate it."
"21880","213 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Abi al-Ash'ath narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - stood to pray; he stood a long standing, then bowed long, then raised his head, then prostrated. Then he stood long, then raised his head, then prostrated. Then he stood less than the standing before it, then bowed less than the bowing before it, then raised his head and prostrated. Then he addressed the people and said: There is nothing I had not been shown but that I have seen, even Paradise and Hell. Then he said: It has been revealed to me that you will be tried in your graves, close to the trial of the False Messiah."
"21881","214 - Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn Harun al-Qazzaz al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she went out after Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr had been killed, leaning upon two of her freed slaves, until she entered upon al-Hajjaj. She said: Is it not time for you to be done with this body and permit us in it so we may conceal it? He said: We still have need of it. She said to her two freed slaves: Take my hand. Indeed, I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: There will emerge from Thaqif a liar and a destroyer - so see which of the two you are. He said: O Allah, a destroyer, not a liar."
"21882","215 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - granted al-Zubayr date-palms as a fief."
"21883","216 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl in the pre-Islamic age used to stand at the Ka'bah, pressing his back against its side, saying: O assembly of Quraysh, I find no one on earth upon the religion of Ibrahim but me. He had abandoned the worship of idols and eating what was slaughtered upon the stone altars, and he used to ransom the buried-alive girl lest she be killed. And Amr ibn Zayd ibn Nufayl said - [the report breaks off here in the source]."
"21884","217 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was asked about Waraqah ibn Nawfal and said: He will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone."
"21885","218 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she used to give out in the time of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - on behalf of her household, the free of them and the enslaved, two mudds of wheat or a sa' of dates, with the mudd by which they took provisions."
"21886","219 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Ubulli narrated to us, Salamah ibn Rawh narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that they used to give the charity of breaking the fast in the time of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - with the mudd by which the people of the house took provisions; all the people of Madinah did that."
"21887","Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Urwah from Asma. 220 - Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Muhajir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mus'ab al-Qarqasani narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: No one is more jealous than Allah."
"21888","221 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she heard the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: Nothing is more jealous than Allah, Blessed and Exalted."
"21889","222 - Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that his mother Asma bint Abi Bakr informed him, that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - upon the pulpit saying: There is nothing more jealous than Allah, Exalted and Majestic."
"21890","223 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman al-Sawwaf narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Urwah - he narrated to him - that Asma bint Abi Bakr narrated to him, that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: Nothing is more jealous than Allah."
"21891","224 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, Harb ibn Shaddad informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Urwah, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: No one is more jealous than Allah."
"21892","225 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il al-Tabudhaki narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - upon the pulpit saying: No one is more jealous than Allah, and for that He forbade indecencies, what is apparent of them and what is hidden."
"21893","Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri from Urwah from Asma. 226 - Abu Yazid Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, from Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ma'afiri, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that when she prepared tharid of anything, she covered it until its steam went, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: That is greater for blessing."
"21894","227 - Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Yazid narrated to us, my father informed me, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid informed me, al-Zuhri narrated to me, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, that he heard Asma bint Abi Bakr saying: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - stood among us and addressed us - and he mentioned the hadith."
"21895","228 - Abu Ja'far al-Tirmidhi Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu al-Hakam al-Laythi narrated to me, he said: My grandfather narrated to me, from his father, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the wives of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - used to wear saffron-dyed shirts while in pilgrim sanctity."
"21896","Abu al-Zinad Abdullah ibn Dhakwan, from Urwa, from Asma. 229 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: My mother came to me at the time of the treaty of Quraysh while she was a polytheist, when they had concluded a treaty with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for their appointed term. She said: So I sought a ruling from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come to me and she is desirous (of gifts); should I maintain ties with her? He said: Yes, maintain ties with your mother."
"21897","Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, the ward of Urwa, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma bint Abi Bakr. 230 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, (ha) and Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us; both said: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The believer sits up in his grave when those who witnessed (his burial) turn away from him, and it is said to him: A man called Muhammad - who is he? If he was a believer, he says: He is the slave of Allah and His Messenger. Then it is said to him: Sleep, may your eyes have restful sleep. And if he was not a believer, he says: By Allah, I do not know; I heard the people saying something so I said it, and they indulged (in talk) so I indulged. Then it is said to him: Sleep, may your eyes have no restful sleep."
"21898","231 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughba narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying toward the Corner, after he had been commanded to proclaim openly what he had been commanded, reciting: ""Then which of the favors of your Lord would you deny?"" while the polytheists were listening."
"21899","Mudrik al-Shami, from Urwa, from Asma. 232 - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mudrik al-Qasri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Khulayd Utba ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, Abu Mudrik reported to me that he heard Urwa ibn al-Zubayr narrating, from his mother Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We slaughtered a horse and we and the household of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate it."
"21900","Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma. 233 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Hakim, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his grandmother - and I do not know whether it was Asma bint Abi Bakr or Su'da bint Awf - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Duba'a bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib and said: ""What prevents you, O aunt, from Hajj?"" She said: I am a sick woman and I fear being detained. He said: Then enter ihram and stipulate: My release (from ihram) is where You detain me."
"21901","Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma. 234 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ya'ish narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention Sidrat al-Muntaha, and he said: ""One hundred riders take shade in the shade of a single branch of it"" - or he said: ""One hundred riders travel in the shade of a branch of it, in which are couches of gold, as though its fruits were large jars."""
"21902","235 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, the author of al-Maghazi, narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, that his father reported to him, from his grandmother Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out, and Abu Bakr set out with him, Abu Bakr carried with him five thousand dirhams - or six thousand dirhams - and went off with it. She said: Then my grandfather Abu Quhafa came to us, and his sight had gone, and said: By Allah, I see he has afflicted you with his wealth along with himself. She said: I said: No, O father, he has left us much good. She said: And I took stones and placed them in a niche in the house in which my father used to keep his money, then I placed a cloth over them, then I took his hand and said: You place your hand on this wealth. She said: So he placed his hand and said: There is no harm if he has left you this wealth. Then he raised his hand and said: If he has left you this, then he has done well, and in this there is sufficiency for you. She said: But by Allah, he had left us nothing; rather, I only wanted to calm the old man with that."
"21903","236 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr reported to me, from his father, from his grandmother Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) halted at Dhu Tuwa, Abu Quhafa said to a young daughter of his among his youngest children: O my little daughter, take me up to (Mount) Abu Qubays. She said: And his sight had been taken away. She said: So she took him up to overlook it, and he said: O my daughter, what do you see? She said: I see a gathered mass of black. He said: That is the cavalry. She said: And I see a man running back and forth among that black mass. He said: That, O my daughter, is the wariz - meaning the one who commands the cavalry - so hurry me back to my house. She said: And the cavalry met him before he reached it. She said: And on the neck of the slave girl was a collar of hers made of silver, and a man met her and snatched it from her neck. Then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makka and entered the mosque, Abu Bakr brought his father leading him. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him, he said: ""Why did you not leave the old man in his house so that I would be the one to come to him?"" Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, he is more deserving of walking to you. So he seated him before him, then wiped his chest and said to him: ""Accept Islam"" - and his head was like a thaghama (a white plant, i.e., completely white). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Change this (white) hair of his."" Then Abu Bakr stood and took his sister by the hand and said: I adjure by Allah and by Islam (that you return) my sister's collar! But no one answered him. So he said: O my little sister, count your collar as (lost) for Allah's sake, for by Allah, trustworthiness today among people is scarce."
"21904","237 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qat'i narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from his father, from Asma, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"21905","238 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: On the day of the Conquest, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Quhafa: ""Accept Islam, you will be safe."""
"21906","239 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us; both said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr was with us. When we were at al-Arj, we dismounted, with A'isha beside him and I beside my father. Abu Bakr sat waiting for his servant boy, and our mount and the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were one and the same. The boy appeared without his camel with him, and Abu Bakr said to him: Where is your camel? He said: I lost it last night. He said: One camel and you lose it? And he began beating him, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: ""Look at this muhrim, what he is doing."""
"21907","Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma. 240 - Abu Zur'a Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the minbar and said: ""O people, the sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they are not eclipsed for the death of anyone nor for his life. When you see that, hasten to prayer and charity and to the remembrance of Allah. And I have seen among you fifty thousand - or seventy thousand, Fulayh doubted - entering Paradise without reckoning, like the image of the moon on the night of full moon."" Then a man stood and said: Supplicate Allah to make me among them. He said: ""O Allah, make him among them. O people, you will never ask me about anything that has been revealed except that I will inform you of it."" Then a man stood and said: Who is my father? He said: ""Your father is so-and-so"" - the father to whom he was attributed."
"21908","Wahb ibn Kaysan Abu Nu'aym, from Asma. 241 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami reported to me, Humayd ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, Wahb ibn Kaysan reported to me, he said: I heard Asma bint Abi Bakr saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was measuring something and counting it, and he said: ""O Asma, do not hoard lest Allah hoard against you."" Asma said: ""So after that day I never hoarded anything that Allah created nor counted it after my day."""
"21909","Al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Asma. 242 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamza al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Hamza narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not hoard lest it be hoarded against you."""
"21910","Mujahid ibn Jabr, from Asma bint Abi Bakr. 243 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr said: Perform Hajj separately (without Umra), and leave the word of your blind men. Abdullah ibn Abbas said: The one whose heart Allah has blinded is you. Will you not ask your mother about this? So he sent to her, and she said: Abdullah ibn Abbas spoke the truth. We set out with the Messenger of Allah as pilgrims, then we made it an Umra, and we exited ihram completely, until the incense burners blazed openly among men and women."
"21911","244 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr said: Perform Hajj separately, and do not listen to the word of your blind men. Ibn Abbas said: The one whose heart Allah has blinded is you. Send to your mother and ask her. So they sent to Asma, and she said: Ibn Abbas spoke the truth. We arrived as pilgrims, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to exit ihram, so we exited ihram completely, until the incense burners blazed openly among men and women."
"21912","What Ibn Abi Mulayka narrated from Asma; Ayyub from Ibn Abi Mulayka. 245 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, that Asma bint Abi Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, I have nothing except what al-Zubayr brings in to me; should I spend from it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Spend, and do not tie (your purse) lest it be tied against you."""
"21913","246 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have no wealth except what al-Zubayr brings into his house for me. He said: ""O Asma, give and give charity, and do not tie (your purse) lest it be tied against you."""
"21914","247 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, he said: Asma bint Abi Bakr reported to me, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I have nothing except from what al-Zubayr brings into his house for me; should I give? He said: ""Do not tie (your purse) lest it be tied against you."""
"21915","248 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not tie (your purse) lest it be tied against you."""
"21916","249 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulayka, he said: Asma bint Abi Bakr reported to me, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have nothing except what al-Zubayr brings into his house; should I give from it? He said: ""Give, and do not tie (your purse) lest it be tied against you."""
"21917","250 - Muhammad ibn Fada' al-Jawhari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I used to serve al-Zubayr, and he had a horse, and I used to tend it; and no service was harder for me than tending the horse. I used to gather fodder for it and look after it. Then I obtained a servant: captives came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave me a servant, and she sufficed me the tending of the horse and relieved me of its burden."
"21918","Nafi' ibn Umar, from Ibn Abi Mulayka. 251 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh, the two Egyptians, narrated to us; both said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi' ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I will be at my Hawd (Pool) until I see who comes to you from me, and people will come short of me. Then I will say: O Lord, my umma, my umma! And He will say: Did you know what they did after you? By Allah, they kept turning back on their heels."" And Ibn Abi Mulayka used to say: ""O Allah, we seek refuge in You from turning back on our heels or changing our religion."""
"21919","252 - Yahya ibn Ayyub and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir narrated to us, with its isnad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the eclipse prayer: he stood and lengthened the standing, then bowed and lengthened the bowing, then rose, then prostrated and lengthened the prostration, then rose, then prostrated and lengthened the prostration, then finished and said: ""Paradise was brought near to me, so that had I ventured upon it I would have brought you a bunch from its bunches, and the Fire drew near to me, until I said: O Lord, and I am among them? And there was a beautiful woman being scratched by a cat. So I said: What is the matter with her? They said: She confined it until it died of hunger; she neither fed it nor let it go to eat."" Nafi' said: I think he said: ""From the grass - or the grasses - of the earth."""
"21920","253 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi' ibn Umar informed us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, he said: Asma bint Abi Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, I have no wealth except what al-Zubayr brings into his house; should I give (some) from it? He said: ""Give as you are able, and do not tie (your purse) lest Allah tie against you."""
"21921","Hammad ibn Yahya al-Abahh, from Ibn Abi Mulayka. 254 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I have no wealth except something that al-Zubayr brings in. He said: ""Give, and do not tie (your purse) lest it be tied against you."""
"21922","Jamil ibn Anbasa Abu al-Nadr al-Basri, from Ibn Abi Mulayka. 255 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, Jamil ibn Anbasa Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Mulayka reporting, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have no wealth to give except what al-Zubayr brings into my house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Asma, give, and do not tie (your purse) lest it be tied against you."""
"21923","Muhammad ibn Sulaym al-Makki, and Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward, from Ibn Abi Mulayka. 256 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sulaym al-Makki and Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: A beggar comes to me; should I give him charity from the house of al-Zubayr without his permission? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Give, and do not tie (your purse) lest it be tied against you."""
"21924","Al-Hajjaj ibn Artat, from Ibn Abi Mulayka. 257 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Al-Hajjaj ibn Artat informed us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is lawful for me from the wealth of al-Zubayr? He said: ""Rutab (fresh dates)"" - meaning food."
"21925","248b - Shu'ayb ibn Imran al-Askari narrated to us, Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Askari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, from Hajjaj, Ibn Abi Mulayka narrated to us, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman entered the Fire because of her cat."
"21926","Khalid Abu Uqayl, from Asma. 259 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh, the two Egyptians, narrated to us; both said: Abu Zayd Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Ghamr narrated to us, Dimam ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Uqayl ibn Khalid, that his father was with al-Hajjaj when he killed Ibn al-Zubayr, so he sent him to Asma bint Abi Bakr and said: Say to her: al-Hajjaj says to you: Separate what wealth of yours there is from the wealth of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. She said: Did he do it to the son of Asma? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will emerge from this tribe of Thaqif two men, one of them lies and the other destroys. As for the liar, we have known him, and I think him to be none but the destroyer. So I returned to him and informed him, and he did not dislike that."
"21927","Abdullah, the freedman of Asma, from Asma. 260 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, Abdullah ibn Muslim, the brother of al-Zuhri, narrated to us, from a freedman of Asma bint Abi Bakr, from Asma, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever among you women believes in Allah and the Last Day, let her not raise her head until we raise our heads - lest they see the private parts of the men because of the shortness of their waist-wrappers; and at that time they wore this striped wrapper."
"21928","261 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Rashid, from Abdullah ibn Muslim, from a freedman of Asma bint Abi Bakr [from Asma bint Abi Bakr], she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O assembly of women, whichever among you believes in Allah and the Last Day, let no woman raise her head until the men raise their heads; and that was because their waist-wrappers were short, fearing that their private parts would become uncovered."
"21929","262 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, the brother of al-Zuhri narrated to us, one who heard Asma bint Abi Bakr informed me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O assembly of believing women, let no woman raise her head before the imam raises his head - because of the tightness of the men's garments."
"21930","263 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami reported to me, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Rashid reporting, from al-Zuhri, from a freedman of Asma bint Abi Bakr, from Asma, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to the women on the minbar: Whoever among you believes in Allah and the Last Day, let her not raise her head until the men raise their heads. She said: Because there was hardship among them, so they wore garments that were short for them, and their private parts would appear."
"21931","264 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Sulayman, from Ata, from Abu Ubaydullah - or Abdullah - the freedman of Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she brought out to him a Tayalisa-style jubba of brocade and said: This is the jubba of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he passed away it was with A'isha, and when A'isha passed away I took it. It is with me; it is washed for the sick person so that cure may be sought with it."
"21932","265 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ata, from a freedman of Asma, he said: We came with Asma to Mina by night, and she said: We used to do that with one who is better than you - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21933","266 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artat, from Abu Umar, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she brought out a jubba fastened with brocade and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear this in war."
"21934","267 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami reported to me, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, Abu Umar, the son-in-law of Ata, narrated to us, from Asma, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"21935","268 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abu Umar, from Asma, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"21936","269 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdullah, the freedman of Asma, informed me, from Asma, that she said on the night of Jam' (Muzdalifa): O my son, has the moon set? - while she was praying, having dismounted at Muzdalifa. I said: No. Then she prayed a while, then said: O my son, has the moon set? He said: And the moon had set; I said: Yes. She said: Then depart. So we departed, then we went on with her until she stoned the Jamra, then she returned and prayed Fajr in her dwelling. I said to her: O dear, you have prayed in the darkness (very early). She said: O my son, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave permission to the weak women."
"21937","270 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abdullah, the freedman of Asma, the like of it."
"21938","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi, from Asma. 271 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Zakariya narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Qays ibn al-Ahnaf al-Thaqafi, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, he said: Asma came with slave girls of hers, and her sight had gone, and said: Where is al-Hajjaj? We said: He is not here. She said: Then order him to order these bones (to be taken down), for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding mutilation. We said: When he comes we will tell him. She said: When he comes, inform him that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will emerge in Thaqif a liar and a destroyer."
"21939","Ya'la ibn Harmala Abu Abi al-Muhayyat, from Asma. 272 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la al-Aslami Abu al-Muhayyat narrated to us, from his father Ya'la ibn Harmala, (ha) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu al-Muhayyat narrated to us, from his father, he said: I arrived in Makka three days after Ibn al-Zubayr had been crucified or killed, and his mother Asma bint Abi Bakr spoke to al-Hajjaj, saying: Has it not come time for this rider to come down? He said: The hypocrite. She said: No, by Allah, he was not a hypocrite; he was indeed fasting (much) and praying at night (much). He said: Be silent, for you are an old woman who has become senile. She said: I have not become senile since I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will emerge from Thaqif a liar and a destroyer. As for the liar, we have seen him - meaning al-Mukhtar - and as for the destroyer, it is you. Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba added: al-Hajjaj said in his hadith: A destroyer of hypocrites."
"21940","273 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu al-Muhayyat narrated to us, from his father, he said: When al-Hajjaj killed Ibn al-Zubayr, al-Hajjaj entered upon Asma bint Abi Bakr and said to her: O mother, the Commander of the Believers has enjoined me regarding you; do you have any need? She said: I have no need of you, nor am I a mother to you; rather, I am the mother of the crucified one. Wait until I report to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will emerge in Thaqif a liar and a destroyer. As for the liar, we have seen him - meaning al-Mukhtar - and as for the destroyer, it is you. Al-Hajjaj said: A destroyer of hypocrites."
"21941","Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab al-Urayji, from Asma. 274 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab reported to me, he said: Al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf crucified Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr on the pass of Madina to show that to Quraysh. When they dispersed, they would pass by without stopping at him, until Abdullah ibn Umar passed and stopped at him and said: Peace be upon you, Abu Khubayb - he said it three times - I forbade you this - he said it three times - you were indeed fasting (much), praying at night (much), joining kinship. That reached al-Hajjaj - the stand of Abdullah ibn Umar - so he had him taken down and threw him in the graves of the Jews, and sent to Asma bint Abi Bakr to come to him, and her sight had gone, but she refused. So he sent to her: You will surely come, or I will send to you one who drags you by your forelocks. She said: By Allah, I will not come to you until you send to me one who drags me by my forelocks. His messenger came to him and informed him. He said: O boy, hand me my sandals. So he handed him his sandals, and he stood, shuffling along, until he came to her. He said to her: How do you see Allah has done with the enemy of Allah? She said: I see you have ruined his world, and he has ruined your Hereafter. As for what you taunted him with, (calling him) Dhat al-Nitaqayn (the one with two waistbands) - yes, I had two waistbands: a waistband with which I covered the food of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from ants, and a waistband which women must have. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: In Thaqif there is a destroyer and a liar. As for the liar, we have known him, and as for the destroyer, you are he. He said: Then he left."
"21942","275 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, from Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, the like of it."
"21943","Abu al-Aliya al-Barra, from Asma. 276 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasna narrated to us, from Abu al-Aliya al-Barra, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that when al-Hajjaj entered upon her, it was said to her: This is the commander al-Hajjaj. She said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Thaqif there is a liar and a destroyer. As for the liar, we have seen him, and as for the destroyer, you are he."
"21944","Muslim al-Qurri, from Asma. 277 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us; both said: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muslim al-Qurri, he said: We entered upon Asma bint Abi Bakr and asked her about mut'a (temporary marriage), and she said: We did it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21945","Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma. 278 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman reported to me, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I was once in a land which the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had granted to Abu Salama and al-Zubayr from the land of al-Nadir. Al-Zubayr went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we had a Jewish neighbor; he slaughtered a sheep and it was cooked, and I smelled its aroma, and I was seized by craving for meat as I had never been seized by anything before, while I was pregnant with a daughter of mine called Khadija. I could not bear it, so I went and entered upon his wife to borrow fire from her, hoping she would feed me, though I had no need of fire. When I smelled its aroma and saw it, my craving increased, so I put it out. Then I came a second time to borrow likewise, then a third. When I saw that, I sat weeping and supplicating Allah. Then the husband of the Jewess came and said: Did anyone enter upon you? She said: No, except the Arab woman who came to borrow fire. He said: I will never eat from it unless you send some of it to her. So she sent me a portion on the bone, and there was nothing on earth more pleasing to me than that meal. Ibn Bukayr said: Al-qadhha is a piece of meat on the bone."
"21946","Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Asma. 279 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Usama ibn Zayd informed me, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, that Asma bint Abi Bakr - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Do not tie (your purse) lest Allah tie against you."
"21947","280 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father reported to me, Waki' narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubayda, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she visited her sister A'isha while al-Zubayr was absent; then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and found the scent of perfume, and said: What (business) does a woman have perfuming herself while her husband is absent?"
"21948","281 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Sha'ir narrated to us, Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama al-Majishun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a person enters his grave, his righteous deed surrounds him: prayer and fasting. The angel comes to him from the direction of prayer and it repels him, and from the direction of fasting and it repels him. Then he calls to him: Sit. So he sits. He says to him: What do you say about this man? He says: Which man? He says: Muhammad. He says: By Allah, I do not know; I heard the people saying something so I said it. The angel says: Upon that you lived, upon it you died, and upon it you will be raised. He said: And there is appointed for him in his grave a black dark beast, with it a whip whose tip is a coal; it strikes him as Allah wills, and none hears its sound to have mercy on him."
"21949","Talha ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Asma. 282 - Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Mu'in ibn Isa narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn Talha, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that when Ibn al-Zubayr was killed, she had something which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given her in a basket, and she lost it; so she ordered it to be sought, and when she found it, she fell prostrate."
"21950","Qays ibn al-Ahnaf, from Asma bint Abi Bakr. 283 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Jarir informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Qays ibn al-Ahnaf, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding mutilation."
"21951","And I heard him saying: From Thaqif, two men: a liar and a destroyer."
"21952","Al-Majishun, from Asma. 284 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Yusuf ibn al-Majishun narrated to us, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to us in Makka twice every day. One day he came to us at midday, and I said: O father, this is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: May my father and mother be ransom for him; nothing has brought him at this hour except some matter. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you felt that Allah has permitted me to emigrate? Abu Bakr said: Companionship, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Companionship. Abu Bakr said: I have two mounts which I have been feeding for such-and-such time in wait for this day; take one of them. He said: For its price, O Abu Bakr. He said: For its price, may my father and mother be ransom for you, if you wish. She said: So we prepared a travel provision for them, then she cut her waistband and tied it with part of it, and they set out and stayed in the cave in Mount Thawr. When they reached it, Abu Bakr entered the cave before him, and left no hole in it except that he put his finger in it, fearing there might be a venomous creature in it. Quraysh went out when they missed them, seeking them, and placed a reward of one hundred camels for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They went around the mountains of Makka until they reached the mountain in which they were. Abu Bakr said to a man he saw facing the cave: O Messenger of Allah, he sees us. He said: No, angels cover us with their wings. That man sat and urinated facing the cave, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he seen us, he would not have done this. They stayed three nights; Amir ibn Fuhayra, the freedman of Abu Bakr, would come to them in the evening with sheep of Abu Bakr, and leave stealthily from them, becoming in the morning with the shepherds in their pastures, and going in the evening with them, stooping in his walk, until when it darkened he would turn with his sheep to them, so the shepherds thought he was with them. And Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr would stay in Makka gathering news, then come to them when it darkened and inform them, then leave stealthily from them and become in the morning in Makka as if he had spent the night there. Then they left the cave and took the coastal route. Abu Bakr would walk in front of him, and when he feared attack from behind, he would walk behind him; his march continued thus. Abu Bakr was a well-known man among people; when someone met him, he would say to Abu Bakr: Who is this with you? He would say: A guide guiding me - meaning guidance in religion - while the other thought him a road guide. Until when they were at the dwellings of Qudayd, which was on their coastal route, a man came to the gathering of Banu Mudlij and said: I have seen two riders toward the coast; I think one of them is the fellow of Quraysh whom they seek. Suraqa ibn Malik said: Those are two riders among those sent in search; he sought to divert the people. Then he called his slave girl and spoke to her secretly, ordering her to bring out his horse and lower his spear and not raise it, until he would come to her in his settled place at such-and-such spot, then come to her. So he rode his horse and went out in their tracks. Suraqa said: I drew near them until I could hear the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then I spurred the horse and it fell on its nostrils. So I took out divining arrows in my quiver and cast lots with them whether to harm him or not; it came out: do not harm him. But my soul refused until I followed him, and I caught up with him at a like spot, and the horse fell. I drew out its leg another time, and cast lots with the arrows whether to harm him or not; it came out: do not harm him. But my soul refused, until when I was at a like spot, I feared the like of what had befallen me would befall me, so I called to him saying: I see you will have a great affair; stop so I may speak to you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped, and he asked him to write for him a guarantee of safety, so he ordered it to be written for him, and it was written for him. Suraqa said: When the day of Hunayn came, I came with the document and brought it out and called: I am Suraqa. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A day of fulfillment. Suraqa said: I likened his leg in its stirrup to nothing but the heart of a palm tree. I mentioned to him something to ask him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man of livestock, and the troughs fill with water and it drinks, then water remains in the troughs and neglected camels come; is there reward for me in that? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, in every moist liver there is reward."
"21953","Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr. Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima: chapter. 285 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about menstrual blood touching the garment, and he said: Scrape it with water, then sprinkle it, and pray in it."
"21954","286 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she said: A woman asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think: if one of us has blood from menstruation touch her garment, what should she do? He said: If blood from menstruation touches one of you, let her scrape it, then let her sprinkle it with water, then let her pray."
"21955","287 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about menstrual blood touching the garment, and he said: Scrape it off, then scrape it with water, then sprinkle it."
"21956","288 - Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about menstrual blood touching the garment, and he said: Scrape it off, then scrape it with water, then sprinkle it."
"21957","289 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the garment struck by blood from menstruation. He said: Let her scrape it, then let her scrape it with water, then let her pray in it."
"21958","290 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the garment of one of us is struck by menstrual blood; what should she do with it? He said: She scrapes it, then scrapes it with water."
"21959","291 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisia narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Faddala informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she informed her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the garment struck by blood from menstruation, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let her scrape it, then let her scrape it, then let her sprinkle it, then let her pray in it."
"21960","292 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father reported to me, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: A woman asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: The garment of one of us is struck by menstrual blood. He said: Let her scrape it, then let her scrape it, then let her sprinkle it with water, and pray in it."
"21961","293 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about menstruation touching the garment of one of us. He said: Take it and scrape it, then scrape it, and sprinkle the rest of your garment."
"21962","294 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about menstrual blood touching the garment, and he said: Scrape it, then scrape it with water, then sprinkle it, and pray in it."
"21963","295 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his wife Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from her grandmother Asma bint Abi Bakr, that a woman asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The garment of one of us is struck by menstrual blood. He said: Let her rub it, then let her scrape it with water, then pray in it."
"21964","296 - Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bazigh narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, one of us menstruates in her garment and sees blood. He said: When one of you sees that in her garment, let her scrape it with water, then let her sprinkle it, and let her pray in it."
"21965","297 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, (ha) and Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamza narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us - both of them - from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"21966","Chapter. 298 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar and al-Thawri, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We slaughtered a horse in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ate its meat."
"21967","299 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We had a horse in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we slaughtered it and ate its meat."
"21968","300 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamza al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We had a horse in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we slaughtered it and ate it."
"21969","301 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir and Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We slaughtered a horse in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were in Madina, and we ate it."
"21970","302 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, (ha) and Ibrahim ibn Na'ila narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma, she said: We slaughtered a horse in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ate it."
"21971","303 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We slaughtered a horse in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ate it."
"21972","304 - Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, Abda ibn Abdullah al-Saffar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Mu'awiya al-Zubayri narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We ate horse meat in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21973","305 - Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Khayyat al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Abu Shayba ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Murri narrated to us, al-Minhal ibn Khalifa narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Salama, from al-Bahiy, the freedman of al-Zubayr, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We had a horse in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we slaughtered it and ate it."
"21974","Chapter. 306 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that a woman of the Ansar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we married off a young girl of ours, and she was ill, and the hair of her head tore out; should we join (extensions to) it? He said: Allah has cursed the woman who joins (hair) and the woman who has it joined."
"21975","307 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his wife Fatima, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about joining (extensions) in hair, and he cursed the woman who joins and the woman who has it joined."
"21976","308 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My daughter is a bride, and she was struck by measles, and her hair tore out; should I join (extensions to) it? He said: Allah has cursed the woman who joins and the woman who has it joined."
"21977","309 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us; both said: Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my daughter is a bride, and she was struck by this ulcer, and her hair tore out; should I join a forelock for her? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed the woman who joins and the woman who has it joined."
"21978","310 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisia narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwa, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, my daughter is a bride, and measles seized her, and her hair fell out; should I join (extensions to) it? He said: Allah has cursed the woman who joins and the woman who has it joined."
"21979","311 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who joins (hair) and the woman who has it joined."
"21980","Chapter. 312 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I entered upon A'isha in her chamber while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with the people. I said: O A'isha, what is the matter with the people? She said: Glory be to Allah, and pointed with her hand. I said: A sign? She said: Glory be to Allah, and nodded with her head, meaning yes - and Abu al-Nu'man nodded with his head."
"21981","313 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, (ha) and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisia narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas and Mufaddal ibn Faddala narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I came to A'isha, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the sun eclipsed; the people were standing praying, and she was standing. I said: What is the matter with the people? She pointed with her hand to the sky and said: Glory be to Allah. I said: A sign? And she pointed, meaning yes. She said: So I stood until faintness came over me, and I began pouring water over my head. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praised Allah and said: There is nothing I had not seen except that I have seen it in this station of mine, even Paradise and the Fire. It has been revealed to me that you will be tried in the graves like - or near to - the trial of the Dajjal - I do not know which of the two she said. One of you will be brought and it will be said: What is your knowledge of this man? As for the believer - or the certain one, I do not know which of the two she said - he will say: Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he brought us clear proofs and guidance, so we answered, believed, and followed. It will be said to him: Sleep righteous. We knew you were a believer. And as for the hypocrite - or the doubter, I do not know which of the two Asma said - he will say: I do not know; I heard the people saying something so I said it."
"21982","314 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with the people. I said to A'isha: What is the matter with the people? She said: Glory be to Allah, and nodded with her head toward the sky. I said: A sign? She nodded with her head, meaning yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and lengthened the standing until dizziness seized me; I drew near the waterskin, opened its mouth, and began pouring over my head. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed until the sun cleared, and some Ansari women clamored, and I began silencing them. I said: O A'isha, what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do? She said: He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed: there is nothing I had not seen except that I have seen it in my station, even Paradise and the Fire. It has been revealed to me that you will be tried in your graves near to - or like - the trial of the Dajjal. One of you will be brought in his grave and it will be said to him: What do you say about this man who was among you? As for the believer, he will say: He is Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah; he brought us clear proofs and guidance, so we answered and followed. It will be said to him: We knew you used to say that, so sleep righteous. And as for the hypocrite doubter, he will say: I do not know. It will be said: You did not know. And he will be treated harshly in his grave."
"21983","315 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I came to A'isha; the people were standing and she was praying. I said: What is the matter with the people? She pointed with her hand to the sky and said: Glory be to Allah. I said: A sign? She pointed with her head, meaning yes. She said: So I stood until faintness overwhelmed me, and I began pouring water over my head. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praised Allah the Mighty and Majestic and extolled Him when he finished, and said: There is nothing I had not seen except that I have seen it in this station of mine, even Paradise and the Fire. It has been revealed to me that you will be tried in the graves like - or near to, I do not know which of the two Asma said - the trial of the False Messiah, the Dajjal. One of you will be brought and it will be said to him: What is your knowledge of this man? The believer - or the certain one, I do not know which of the two Asma said - will say: He is Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah; he brought us clear proofs and guidance, so we answered and followed. It will be said: We knew you were a believer in him - saying it three times. And as for the hypocrite - or the doubter, I do not know which of the two Asma said - he will say: I heard the people saying something so I said it."
"21984","316 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Usama and Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us - all of them - from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I came to A'isha; the people were standing and she was praying. I said: What is the matter with the people? She pointed with her hand toward the sky and said: Glory be to Allah. I said: A sign? She pointed with her head, meaning yes. So I stood until faintness overwhelmed me, and I began pouring water over my head. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praised Allah and extolled Him as He deserves, and said: There is nothing I was shown except that I saw it in this station of mine, even Paradise and the Fire. It has been revealed to me that you will be tried in the graves like - or near to, I do not know which of the two Asma said - the trial of the False Messiah. One of you will be brought and it will be said to him: What is your knowledge of this man? As for the believer, he will say: Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he brought us clear proofs and guidance, so we answered and followed. It will be said: Sleep righteous, for we knew you believed in Allah. And as for the hypocrite - or the doubter, I do not know which of the two she said - he will say: I do not know; I heard the people saying something so I said it."
"21985","317 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamza narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"21986","Chapter. 318 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to free slaves when the sun eclipsed."
"21987","319 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'ida narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded freeing slaves at the eclipse of the sun."
"21988","320 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Ghannam ibn Ali narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma, she said: We were commanded to free slaves at the eclipse of the sun."
"21989","321 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Urwa and Fatima bint al-Mundhir, that both said: Asma bint Abi Bakr emigrated while she was pregnant with Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr; she arrived at Quba and gave birth to Abdullah there. Then she went out after giving birth to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to have him do tahnik for him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took him from her and placed him in his lap, then called for a date. A'isha said: We stayed a while seeking it before we found it. He chewed it, then placed it in his mouth; the first thing to enter his stomach was the saliva of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Asma said: Then he wiped him, supplicated for him, and named him Abdullah. Then he came later, when he was seven or eight years old, to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); al-Zubayr ordered him to do that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled when he saw him coming toward him, then pledged him."
"21990","Chapter. 322 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that a woman asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, I have a fellow-wife - meaning a co-wife, but she disliked saying co-wife - so is there sin upon me if I claim to be satiated with what I was not given? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who claims to be satiated with what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood."
"21991","323 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisia and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us; both said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that a woman said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a husband, and I have a fellow-wife (co-wife); is there sin upon me if I claim to be satiated before her with what my husband did not give me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: The one who claims to be satiated with what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood."
"21992","324 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a co-wife; is there sin upon me if I claim to be satiated from my husband with what he does not give me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who claims to be satiated with what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood."
"21993","325 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ila al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who claims to be satiated with what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood."
"21994","326 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who claims to be satiated with what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood."
"21995","327 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamza narrated to us, my father reported to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who claims to be satiated with what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood."
"21996","328 - Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwa narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who claims to be satiated with what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood."
"21997","Chapter. 329 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that when a fever-stricken woman was brought to her, she ordered water to be poured over her, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cool it with water, for it is from the heat of Hell."
"21998","330 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that when a woman who had fever was brought to her, she called for water and poured it over her and between her sides, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to cool it with water, saying: It is from the fierce heat of Hell."
"21999","331 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us; both said: Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that a fever-stricken woman would be brought to her, and she would call for water and pour it on her side, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cool it with water, saying: It is from the fierce heat of Hell."
"22000","332 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, that Asma, when a woman who had fever was brought to her, would call for water for her, take water and pour it between her and her side, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to cool it with water."
"22001","333 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, (ha) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, that Asma bint Abi Bakr, when a woman who had fever was brought to her, would call for water for her, take water and pour it between her and her side, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fever is from the fierce heat of Hell, so cool it with water."
"22002","334 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: I read to Anas ibn Iyad, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa reported to me, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, that Asma bint Abi Bakr, when a fever-stricken woman who had fever was brought to her, would call for water for her, take water and pour it between her and her side, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her to cool it with water."
"22003","335 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that a fever-stricken woman would be brought to her, and she would order water and pour it over her, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to cool it with water."
"22004","336 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamza narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma, that when a fever-stricken woman was brought to her, she ordered water to be poured over her, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water."
"22005","Chapter. 337 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Spend, O Asma, and give handfuls like this, and like this, and like this; and do not count lest Allah count against you."
"22006","338 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give freely, spend, and give handfuls; do not count lest it be counted against you, and do not tie (your purse) lest it be tied against you."
"22007","339 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us - both of them - from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Spend, give handfuls, and do not count lest it be counted against you."
"22008","Chapter. 340 - Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwa narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a dream after his death, and I saw him saying: Has the Qur'an been distorted, O Asma? I said: Thus, may my father and mother be ransom for you - the distorter and the upright one. He repeated that to me several times; each time I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you - the distorter and the upright one. Then he said to me: How are your sons? I said: O Messenger of Allah, they are seized with a severe seizure. I saw him look at one of his wives, as though she were Hafsa bint Umar, and he said: Give her a cure for her two sons; as for poison, I do not cure from it. I saw her give me a black grain like nigella, or like leek seed, red earth, and a string of pearls. She said: When one of the children of Asma among all the tribes fell ill, a cup would be taken and filled with water, then red earth, leek seed, nigella, and a string of pearls would be placed in it, then that water would be poured over him."
"22009","Chapter. 341 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: My mother came to me while she was a polytheist, and I sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to maintain ties with her. He said: Maintain ties with her."
"22010","342 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: My mother came to me while she was a polytheist, in the time of Quraysh and their truce in which they had made a treaty with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come to me and she is desirous; should I maintain ties with her? He said: Yes, maintain ties with your mother."
"22011","343 - Yusuf al-Qadi and Ibrahim ibn Na'ila al-Asbahani narrated to us; both said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna and Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: My mother came to me in the time of Quraysh while she was a polytheist, and I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Should I maintain ties with her? He said: Yes."
"22012","Chapter. 344 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ali ibn Umar narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father and Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that when Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr was born, he was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he wiped him, supplicated for him, and named him Abdullah. Then he came later, when he was seven or eight years old, to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); al-Zubayr ordered him to do that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled when he saw him coming and pledged him."
"22013","Chapter. 345 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We broke fast in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a cloudy day, then the sun appeared. It was said to Hisham: Were they ordered to make up? He said: There is no escape from that."
"22014","346 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: Fast was broken in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a cloudy day, then the sun appeared. It was said to Hisham: Were they ordered to make up? He said: There is no escape from it."
"22015","Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir. 347 - Abu Zur'a Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from her grandmother Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I heard a woman asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, I married off my daughter, and she was struck by this ulcer - smallpox or measles - and her hair fell out. She has recovered, and her husband has urged us for her, but there is no hair on her head; should we place something on her head to beautify her with? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed the woman who joins (hair) and the woman who has it joined."
"22016","348 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while a woman asked him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, I married off my daughter, and she was struck by this ulcer - smallpox or measles - and her hair fell out from it. Then she recovered, and her husband has urged us for her, but there is no hair on her head; should we place something on her head to beautify her with? He said: Allah has cursed the woman who joins and the woman who has it joined."
"22017","349 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who joins (hair) and the woman who has it joined."
"22018","350 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father reported to me, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - a woman asked him about menstrual blood touching her clothes, and he said: Wash it with water, then sprinkle it on the rest of your garment, and pray in it."
"22019","351 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she heard a woman asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I have a co-wife, and I claim to be satiated from my husband with what does not reach me, to anger her with that; is there anything upon me in that? He said: The one who claims to be satiated with what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood."
"22020","Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, from Fatima. 352 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We used to give Zakat al-Fitr in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the mudd with which we sustained ourselves."
"22021","Safiyya bint Shayba ibn Uthman al-Hajabiyya, from Asma. 353 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman reported to me, from his mother Safiyya bint Shayba, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alarmed on the day the sun eclipsed; he took a coat of mail and wore it until a cloak was brought to him. He stood with the people a long standing: he would stand, then bow, then rise; had a man come after he rose, he would not have known he had bowed anything, nor would it have occurred to him that he had bowed, because of the length of the standing. I began looking at the woman who was older and the woman who was sicker than me standing, saying: I am more deserving of enduring the long standing."
"22022","354 - Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham al-Mu'adhdhin narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from his mother Safiyya bint Shayba, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We set out in ihram, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, let him remain in his ihram; and whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him exit ihram. I did not have a sacrificial animal with me, so I exited ihram, while al-Zubayr had one with him, so he did not exit ihram. I put on my clothes, then came and sat beside al-Zubayr. He said: Get up from me. I said: Do you fear I will pounce on you?"
"22023","355 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Imran ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Safiyya, from his mother, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We set out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising the talbiya for Hajj, and he said to us: Whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, let him remain in his ihram; and whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him shave (i.e., exit ihram)."
"22024","356 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ila al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman and Abu Ma'shar al-Barra narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Safiyya, from his mother, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that they arrived with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Makka."
"22025","357 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar al-Barra narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Safiyya, from his mother, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I married off my daughter; she fell ill and her head shed its hair, and her husband has come to me repeatedly; should I join (extensions to) her hair? He cursed the woman who joins and the woman who has it joined."
"22026","Asma bint Umays al-Khath'amiyya, among the emigrant women. 358 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, concerning the naming of those who emigrated to the land of Abyssinia: Ja'far ibn Abi Talib, and with him his wife Asma bint Umays al-Khath'amiyya; she bore for him in the land of Abyssinia Abdullah ibn Ja'far, Awn ibn Ja'far, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far."
"22027","359 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: We entered upon Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, in his illness, and saw a fair woman with tattooed hands fanning him; she was Asma bint Umays."
"22028","360 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Uqba informed me, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believing sisters are: Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Umm al-Fadl, the wife of al-Abbas; Asma bint Umays, the wife of Ja'far; and the wife of Hamza - she is their sister through their mother."
"22029","What Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated from Asma - what Asma bint Umays transmitted. 361 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Farrukh informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sa'id ibn Uqba al-Zuraqi, from Zur'a ibn Abdullah ibn Ziyad, that Umar ibn al-Khattab reported to him, from Asma, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while she had shubrum (a purgative plant) which she was pounding. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What are you doing with this? She said: O Prophet of Allah, I give it to drink to so-and-so. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a disease (harmful). Then he entered upon her while she had senna with her, and said: What are you doing with this? She said: So-and-so drinks it. He said: If anything should ward off death, senna would ward it off."
"22030","What Ibn Abbas narrated from Asma. 362 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yahya ibn al-Ala al-Razi, from his uncle Shu'ayb ibn Khalid, from Hanzala ibn Sabra ibn al-Musayyib ibn Najiya, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Fatima would be mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but no one mentioned her except that he turned away from him, until they despaired of her. Sa'd ibn Mu'adh met Ali and said: By Allah, I do not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) withholding her except for you. Ali said to him: Why do you think that? By Allah, I am not one of the two men: I am not a man of worldly means seeking what is with me - and he knows I have neither yellow (gold) nor white (silver) - nor am I the disbeliever who is softened with her away from his religion - meaning, won over with her. I am the first to accept Islam. Sa'd said: I adjure you to relieve me of it, for I have relief in that. He said: What should I say? He said: Say: I have come as a suitor to Allah and His Messenger for Fatima bint Muhammad. So Ali went and presented himself to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was burdened and reserved, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: It is as though you have a need, O Ali? He said: Yes, I have come to you as a suitor to Allah and His Messenger for Fatima bint Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Welcome - a faint word. Ali returned to Sa'd ibn Mu'adh and said: I did what you ordered me, but he only welcomed me with a faint word. Sa'd said: He has married you to her, by the One who sent him with the truth; there is no breaking now nor lying. I adjure you to come to him tomorrow and say: O Messenger of Allah, when will you consummate my marriage? Ali said: This is harder for me than the first; shall I not first state my need? He said: Say as I commanded you. So Ali went and said: O Messenger of Allah, when will you consummate my marriage? He said: Tomorrow, if Allah wills. Then he called Bilal and said: O Bilal, I have married my daughter to my cousin, and I love that it be among the sunna of my umma to have food at marriage; so go to the sheep, take a sheep and four or five mudds, and make for me a bowl - perhaps I may gather the Muhajirun and the Ansar. When you finish it, inform me. He went and did what he ordered him, then brought a bowl and placed it before him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pierced into its top, then said: Bring the people in to me in groups, group after group, and do not pass from one group to another - meaning, when you finish with one group, do not return a second time. The people began coming; whenever one group finished, another would come, until the people finished. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to some remainder of it, spat in it, and blessed it, saying: O Bilal, carry it to your mothers and say to them: Eat and feed whoever visits you. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood until he entered upon the women and said: I have married my daughter to my cousin; you know her station with me, and I am handing her to him, so here is your daughter. The women stood to her, perfumed her from their perfume, dressed her from their clothes, and adorned her from their jewelry. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered; when the women saw him they leapt up, with a curtain between them and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Asma bint Umays stayed behind. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: As you are; at your ease - who are you? She said: I am the one who guards your daughter; the girl on the night she is taken to her husband must have a woman near her - if she has a need or wants something, she confides that to her. He said: I ask my God to guard you from before you, behind you, on your right, and on your left, from the accursed Satan. Then he called for Fatima, and she came forward. When she saw Ali sitting beside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she became reserved and wept. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) feared her weeping was because Ali had no wealth, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What makes you weep? I have not stinted you concerning myself, and I have secured for you the best of my family. By the One in whose hand is my soul, I have married you to one blessed in this world, and in the Hereafter he is among the righteous. She softened from that. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Asma, bring me the washbasin and fill it with water. Asma brought him the washbasin and filled it with water. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped himself in it and washed his feet and face, then called Fatima, took a handful of water and struck it on her head, and a handful before her, then sprinkled his skin and her skin. Then he embraced them and said: O Allah, they are from me and I am from them. O Allah, as You have removed impurity from us and purified me, purify them. Then he called for another washbasin, then called Ali and did with him as he did with her, then supplicated for him as he supplicated for her, then said: Go to your house; may Allah join you, bless your journey, and set right your affairs. Then he stood and closed the door upon them with his hand. Ibn Abbas said: Asma bint Umays informed me that she watched the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicating for them specifically, associating no one with them in his supplication, until he disappeared into his chamber."
"22031","Abdullah ibn Ja'far Dhi al-Janahayn, from his mother Asma. 363 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Hilal, a freedman of theirs, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from his mother Asma bint Umays, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me words to say at distress: There is no god but Allah, my Lord; I associate nothing with Him."
"22032","Abu Yazid al-Madini, from Asma. 364 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, (ha) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, my father reported to me, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Yazid al-Madini, from Asma bint Umays, she said: I was at the wedding celebration of Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). In the morning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and knocked on the door; Umm Ayman stood to him and opened the door for him. He said: O Umm Ayman, call my brother for me. She said: Your brother - a Yemeni expression - and you marry him your daughter? He said: O Umm Ayman, call for me. The women heard the voice of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and crowded together, sitting in a corner. Then Ali came; he supplicated for him and sprinkled water on him from it. Then he said: Call Fatima for me. She came, sweaty - or shy - from modesty. He said to her: Be silent; I have married you to the most beloved of my household to me. He supplicated for her and called for water and sprinkled it on her. Then he went out and saw a dark figure, saying: Who is this? She said: Asma. He said: The daughter of Umays? I said: Yes. He said: Were you at the wedding celebration of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), honoring him? I said: Yes. So he supplicated for me."
"22033","365 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ikrima and Abu Yazid al-Madini - or one of them, Abd al-Razzaq doubted - that Asma bint Umays said: When Fatima was taken to Ali ibn Abi Talib, we found in his house nothing but spread sand, a cushion stuffed with fiber, a jar, and a mug. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Ali: Do not initiate anything - or he said: Do not approach your wife until I come to you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Is my brother there? Umm Ayman said - she is the mother of Usama ibn Zayd, she was Abyssinian, and she was a righteous woman: O Messenger of Allah, is this your brother, yet you married him your daughter? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had made brotherhood among his Companions, and made brotherhood between Ali and himself. He said: That is so, O Umm Ayman. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a vessel with water in it, said in it what Allah willed him to say, then wiped with it the chest of Ali and his face. Then he called Fatima; she stood to him, stumbling in her cloak from modesty. He sprinkled on her from that, and said to her what Allah willed him to say. Then he said to her: I have not stinted you in marrying you to the most beloved of my family to me. Then he saw a dark figure behind the curtain - or behind the door - and said: Who is this? She said: Asma. He said: Asma bint Umays? She said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Did you come honoring the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his daughter? She said: Yes; the girl on the night she is taken to her husband must have a woman near her - if she has a need, she confides that to her. She said: He supplicated for me with a supplication; it is my most trusted deed with me. Then he said to Ali: Here is your wife. Then he went out and turned away. She said: He kept supplicating for them until he disappeared into his chamber."
"22034","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, from Asma. 366 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Asma bint Umays, that she gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at al-Bayda; Abu Bakr mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Command her to bathe, then enter ihram."
"22035","367 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Abu al-Hasan al-Ubulli, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Asma bint Umays, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: O daughter of Umays, there is no ghusl upon you women, no Friday (prayer), no shaving, no shortening - except that one of you take for herself, or whoever of her (party) is in a state of sanctity, from the ends of her hair at the front of her head on the Day of Sacrifice when she performs Hajj."
"22036","368 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Abi al-Muhajir narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Asma bint Umays, that she gave birth at Dhu al-Hulayfa; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her to bathe and enter ihram."
"22037","Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Asma. 369 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, Asim ibn Ali, and Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us; they said: Muhammad ibn Talha ibn Musarrif narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utayba, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Asma bint Umays, she said: When Ja'far was struck (martyred), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me, saying: Remain (without adornment) three days, then do what you wish."
"22038","Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma bint Umays. 370 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma bint Umays, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh has had prolonged bleeding for such-and-such time and has not prayed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glory be to Allah, this is from Satan. Let her sit in a tub; when she sees yellowness above the water, let her bathe once for Zuhr and Asr, bathe once for Maghrib and Isha, then perform ablution between that."
"22039","371 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Mu'adh al-San'ani narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Asma bint Umays used to report that Umar ibn al-Khattab, upon their arrival from the land of Abyssinia, came taunting them for staying in the land of Abyssinia. She said: I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: You are not like that."
"22040","Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Asma bint Umays. 372 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed me, from Asma bint Umays, she said: The first (symptoms) of the illness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appeared in the house of Maymuna; his illness intensified until he fainted. She said: His wives consulted about forcing medicine into his mouth, so they forced it. When he regained consciousness, he said: What is this? Is it the doing of women who came from here - and he pointed with his hand toward the land of Abyssinia. Asma bint Umays was among them. They said: We suspected you had pleurisy, O Messenger of Allah. He said: That is a disease Allah would never afflict me with. Let none remain in the house except that he is forced (medicine) - except the uncle of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - meaning Abbas. He said: Maymuna was forced that day while she was fasting, by the firm resolve of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22041","Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib from Asma bint Umays. 373 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to me, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Kathir, he said: Abdullah ibn Muslim, the keeper of the mushafs, informed me that Kilab ibn Talid, one of Banu Layth, while he was sitting with Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, a messenger of Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im came to him saying: Your maternal aunt sends salam to you and says: How is the hadith you narrated to me from Asma bint Umays? Sa'id said: Inform him that Asma informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: None endures the hardship and severity of Madinah except that I will be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"22042","374 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Warraq narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Asma bint Umays, that she gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at Dhu al-Hulayfah, so Abu Bakr asked the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and he commanded him to order her to bathe and enter ihram."
"22043","Mujahid ibn Jabr from Asma. 375 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Asma bint Umays, that she came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - with the two sons of Ja'far and said: People have struck down your brother's two sons. He said: Then seek ruqyah for them."
"22044","Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Asma. 376 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Ata informed me, from Asma bint Umays, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - looked at her sons, the sons of Ja'far, and said: Why are their bodies thin? She said: The evil eye quickly befalls them; shall I perform ruqyah for them? He said: With what? So she presented to him words in which there was no harm, and he said: Perform ruqyah for them."
"22045","Abdullah ibn Babayh from Asma bint Umays. 377 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Abi Najih, from Abdullah ibn Babayh, from Asma bint Umays, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the evil eye quickly befalls the sons of Ja'far; shall I seek ruqyah for them? He said: Yes, seek ruqyah for them, for if I were to say that anything outruns the decree, I would say that the evil eye outruns it."
"22046","Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah al-Zuraqi from Asma bint Umays. 378 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Abdullah, that he heard Ibrahim ibn Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah al-Ansari reporting, from his father, from Asma bint Umays, that she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered one day upon A'ishah bint Abi Bakr, and with her was her sister Asma, wearing loose garments with wide sleeves. When the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - looked at her, he stood up and went out. A'ishah said to her: Step aside, for the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - has seen in you something he disliked. Then she opened, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered, and A'ishah asked him why he stood up. He said: Have you not seen her appearance? It is not for the Muslim woman that anything of her should show except like this. And he took his two sleeves and covered with them the backs of his hands until nothing of his hands showed except his fingers, then he placed his hands upon his temples until nothing showed except his face."
"22047","379 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Urwah ibn Amir, from Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah, from Asma bint Umays, that she said to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -: The sons of Ja'far are struck by the evil eye; shall I seek ruqyah for them? He said: Yes; if anything were to outrun the decree, the evil eye would outrun it."
"22048","Umm Ja'far bint Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Talib from her grandmother Asma. 380 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, the author of al-Maghazi, narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, from Umm Isa, from Umm Ja'far bint Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Talib, from her grandmother Asma bint Umays, she said: When Ja'far and his companions were struck, the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon me while I had kneaded their dough, washed my sons, oiled them and cleaned them. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Bring me the sons of Ja'far. She said: So I brought them to him, and he kissed them and his eyes shed tears. I said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransomed for you, what makes you weep? Has anything reached you about Ja'far and his companions? He said: Yes, they were struck today. She said: So I stood up wailing, and the women gathered to me, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - went out to his family and said: Do not neglect the family of Ja'far by preparing food for them, for they are occupied with the affair of their companion."
"22049","381 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, from Umm Isa al-Jazzar, she said: Umm Awn bint Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed me, from her grandmother Asma bint Umays, that she said: On the day on which Ja'far was struck, the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came to me, then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Ibrahim ibn Sa'd."
"22050","382 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Fitri informed me, from Awn ibn Muhammad, from Umm Ja'far, from Asma bint Umays, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - prayed Zuhr at al-Sahba, then he sent Ali for a need. He returned after the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - had prayed Asr. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - placed his head in Ali's lap and slept, and he did not move him until the sun had set. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: O Allah, Your servant Ali detained himself for Your Prophet, so return the sun for him. She said: So the sun rose over him until it was lifted over the mountains and the earth, and Ali stood, performed ablution and prayed Asr, then it set; and that was at al-Sahba."
"22051","383 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Fitri narrated to me, from Awn ibn Muhammad, from his mother Umm Ja'far, from her grandmother Asma, she said: Your grandmother Fatimah was given in marriage to your grandfather Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both; the stuffing of her mattress and her pillow was nothing but palm fiber. Ali held a wedding feast for Fatimah, and his feast in those days was no better than his feast: he pawned his armor with a Jew for half a measure of barley."
"22052","Fatimah bint al-Husayn from Asma. 384 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih and Ja'far ibn Ziyad al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Musa al-Juhani, from Fatimah bint al-Husayn, from Asma bint Umays, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, but there is no prophet after me."
"22053","385 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from Musa al-Juhani, from Fatimah bint al-Husayn, from Asma bint Umays, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say to Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa."
"22054","386 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Mus'ab al-Ushnani narrated to us, Isa ibn Uthman al-Kisa'i narrated to us, Yahya ibn Isa narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Hazim, from Musa al-Juhani, from Fatimah bint Ali, she said: I heard Asma bint Umays say: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say to Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."
"22055","387 - Abu Husayn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Jandal ibn Waliq narrated to us, Hafs ibn Imran narrated to us, from Musa al-Juhani, from Fatimah bint al-Husayn, from Asma bint Umays, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say to Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."
"22056","388 - Abu Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, Umar ibn Sa'd al-Basri narrated to us, from Musa al-Juhani, from Fatimah bint al-Husayn, from Asma bint Umays, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."
"22057","389 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Musa al-Juhani, he said: I heard Fatimah bint al-Husayn say: Asma bint Umays narrated to me that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: O Ali, you are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."
"22058","390 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (ha). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they both said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan, from Fatimah bint Husayn, from Asma bint Umays, she said: Revelation would come to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while his head was in Ali's lap, and he did not pray Asr until the sun had set. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: O Allah, Ali was in obedience to You and obedience to Your Messenger, so return the sun for him. Asma said: I saw it set, and I saw it rise after it had set. And the wording is that of the hadith of Uthman."
"22059","391 - Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan, from Fatimah bint Ali, from Asma bint Umays, she said: When revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - he would almost be overcome, and it descended upon him one day while he was in Ali's lap. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to him: Have you prayed Asr, O Ali? He said: No, O Messenger of Allah. So he supplicated to Allah, and He returned the sun for him until he prayed Asr. She said: I saw the sun rise after it had set, when it was returned until he prayed Asr."
"22060","Hurrah from Asma bint Umays. 392 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (ha). And Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, they both said: Abu al-Jawwab al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from Harun ibn Sa'd, from Abi al-Safar, from Hurrah, from Asma bint Umays, she said: Ali proposed to me, and that reached the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - so he said: It was not for her to harm Allah and His Messenger."
"22061","Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Asma bint Umays. 393 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, he said: Umar said to Asma bint Umays: We preceded you in hijrah. She said: Yes indeed, by Allah, you preceded us; we were with the barefoot naked ones, while you were with the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - teaching your ignorant, instructing your learned, and commanding you to noble morals."
"22062","Amir al-Sha'bi from Asma bint Umays. 394 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from al-Sha'bi, from Asma bint Umays, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, some people claim that we are not among the female emigrants. He said: Whoever says that has lied; you have two hijrahs: you emigrated to al-Najashi, and you emigrated to me."
"22063","Habib ibn Salim from Asma bint Umays. 395 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Asad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Harun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abi Umar, from Habib ibn Salim, from Asma, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Part of a man's wretchedness in this world is three things: a bad house, a bad wife, and a bad mount. She said: O Messenger of Allah, what is a bad house? He said: Its narrow courtyard and its evil neighbors. It was said: What is a bad mount? He said: Withholding its back, and its bad rib. It was said: What is a bad wife? He said: Barrenness of her womb, and badness of her character."
"22064","Abu al-Uyuf al-Anazi from Asma bint Umays. 396 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Mujammi' ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu al-Uyuf Sa'b or Su'ayb al-Anazi narrated to me, he said: I heard Asma bint Umays say: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - with these two ears of mine say: Whoever is struck by worry, grief, illness or hardship and says: Allah is my Lord, He has no partner, it will be removed from him."
"22065","Utbah ibn Abdullah al-Taymi, freedman of Ma'mar, from Asma. 397 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Zur'ah ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of Ma'mar al-Taymi, from Asma bint Umays, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to me: With what were you taking laxatives? I said: With shubrum. He said: That is hot, hot. I said: Then I took senna as a laxative. He said: If anything were to heal from death, it would be senna."
"22066","398 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Utbah ibn Abdullah al-Taymi narrated to me, from Asma bint Umays, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - asked her: With what do you take laxatives? She said: I used to take shubrum as a laxative. He said: Hot, hot. She said: Then I took senna as a laxative. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: If there were healing from death in anything, it would be in senna."
"22067","Dawud ibn Abi Asim al-Thaqafi from Asma bint Umays. 399 - Abu Aqil Anas ibn Salim al-Khawlani narrated to us, Amr ibn Hisham Abu Umayyah al-Harrani narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tara'ifi narrated to us, from Ali ibn Urwah, from Abd al-Malik, from Dawud ibn Abi Asim, from Asma bint Umays, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Half of what is dug for my ummah of graves is from the evil eye."
"22068","Abu Shaddad from Mujahid from Asma. 400 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar ibn Faris narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Abi Shaddad, from Mujahid, he said: Asma bint Umays said: I was the companion of A'ishah who prepared her and brought her in to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - with women along with me. We found nothing but a cup of milk, so he drank from it, then handed it to the girl, and she felt shy. I said: Do not turn back the hand of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. So the girl drank, then he said: Hand it to your companions. They said: We do not desire it. He said: Do not combine lying and hunger. I said: If one of us says of something she desires that she does not desire it, is that counted as lying? He said: Lying is written as lying, until even the lie is written as a lie."
"22069","Zayd al-Khath'ami from Asma bint Umays. 401 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hashim al-Kufi narrated to us, Zayd al-Khath'ami narrated to me, from Asma bint Umays al-Khath'amiyyah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Evil is the servant, a servant who behaves tyrannically and transgresses and forgets the All-Compelling, the Most High. Evil is the servant, a servant who is miserly and arrogant and forgets the Great, the Most Exalted. Evil is the servant, a servant who amuses himself and is heedless and forgets the beginning and the end. Evil is the servant, a servant who wrongs and rebels and forgets the graves and decay. Evil is the servant, a servant who seeks the world through religion. Evil is the servant, a servant who seeks religion through doubts. Evil is the servant, a servant whom fear humiliates and removes from the truth. Evil is the servant, a servant whom greed leads. Evil is the servant, a servant who has a desire that misguides him."
"22070","An unnamed man from Asma bint Umays. 402 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, he said: One of our companions narrated to me, from Asma bint Umays, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon her for one of his needs, then went out, and she complained to him of need. He said: How will it be with you when you are tested by a servant for whom the rivers and fruits of the earth have been made subservient, so whoever follows him, he feeds him and makes him disbelieve, and whoever disobeys him, he deprives him and withholds from him? I said: O Messenger of Allah, a young girl is kept at the oven for an hour baking it, and I almost fall into trial in my prayer; how will it be with us when that happens? He said: Allah will protect the believers on that day with what He protects the angels: glorification. Between his eyes is written disbeliever; every believer, literate and illiterate, will read it."
"22071","Asma bint Yazid ibn al-Sakan al-Ansariyyah. 403 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muhajir and Amr ibn Muhajir, from their father, that Asma bint Yazid ibn al-Sakan, the cousin of Mu'adh ibn Jabal, killed nine of the Romans on the day of Yarmuk with the pole of her tent."
"22072","What Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated from Asma bint Yazid. Qatadah ibn Di'amah from Shahr ibn Hawshab. 404 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid al-Ansariyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was in my house, and he mentioned the Dajjal, saying: Before him are three years: a year in which the sky withholds a third of its rain and the earth a third of its vegetation, the second in which the sky withholds two-thirds of its rain and the earth two-thirds of its vegetation, and the third in which the sky withholds all its rain and the earth its vegetation, so no tooth-bearing nor hoofed beast among animals remains except it perishes. Among his severest trial is that he comes to the Bedouin and says: If I bring your camels back to life for you, do you not know that I am your lord? He says: Yes. So Satan appears to him in the form of his camels at their best in udders and greatest in humps. And he comes to a man whose brother has died and whose father has died, and says: If I bring your father and your brother back to life for you, do you not know that I am your lord? He says to him: Yes. So Satan appears to him in the form of his father and his brother. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - went out for a need, then returned while the people were anxious and grieved by what he had told them. He took hold of the door and said: What is the matter? Asma said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, you have torn our hearts with the mention of the Dajjal. He said: If he emerges while I am alive, I will dispute against him, otherwise my Lord is my deputy over every believing Muslim. Asma said: I said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we knead our dough and go hungry before we bake it; how will the believers fare on that day? He said: What suffices the people of heaven of glorification and sanctification will suffice them."
"22073","405 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, Qatadah and Hajjaj ibn al-Aswad, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was among a group of his Companions, and they mentioned the Dajjal. He said: Before the Hour are red drought years: in the first year a third of the rain of the sky and a third of the vegetation of the earth are withheld, in the second year the sky withholds two-thirds of its rain and the earth two-thirds of its vegetation, and in the third year the sky withholds its rain and the earth its vegetation, until no hoofed nor cloven-hoofed one remains. Then he went out for his need, then returned while they were wailing. He took hold of the two sides of the door and said: What is the matter with you? They said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us kneads his dough and cannot wait until it ferments. He said: If he emerges while I am among you, I will dispute against him, otherwise Allah is my deputy over every believer. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what will suffice the believer on that day? He said: What suffices the angels of glorification, praise, tahlil and takbir."
"22074","406 - Abu Shu'ayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to me, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, Asma bint Yazid ibn al-Sakan, the cousin of Mu'adh, narrated to me, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came to me with a group of his Companions, and he mentioned the Dajjal. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Before his emergence are three years, or a year: the sky withholds a third of its rain and the earth a third of its vegetation, in the second year the sky withholds two-thirds of its rain and the earth two-thirds of its vegetation, and in the third year the sky withholds what is in it and the earth what is in it, so every tooth-bearing and hoofed one perishes. Among his severest trial is that he says to the Bedouin: If I bring your camels back to life for you, great in udders, long in humps, stout - do you know that I am your lord? He says: Yes. So Satan appears to him. Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - went out for one of his needs, and I placed his ablution water for him, and the people wept until their voices rose. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - took hold of the door and said: What is the matter? We said: O Messenger of Allah, you have torn their hearts with the Dajjal. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: If the Dajjal emerges while I am alive, I will dispute against him; if I die, Allah is my deputy over every believer. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what will suffice the believers on that day? He said: What suffices the people of heaven: glorification and sanctification will suffice them."
"22075","407 - Ishaq ibn Jamil al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: We were with the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - in a house, and he said: When before the emergence of the Dajjal the sky withholds a third of its rain for three years, and the earth withholds a third of its vegetation; in the second year the sky withholds two-thirds of its rain and the earth two-thirds of its vegetation; in the third year the sky withholds its rain and the earth all its vegetation. Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of al-Awza'i."
"22076","408 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and he mentioned the like of it."
"22077","409 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: I went with my brother to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while wearing two gold bracelets, and he said: Would it please you for Allah to encircle you with two bracelets of fire? So I pulled them off and threw them away, and I do not know which of the people took them."
"22078","410 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, that she came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while her maternal aunt wore two bracelets, and he mentioned the like of it."
"22079","Thabit al-Bunani from Shahr ibn Hawshab. 411 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani informed us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - recited this verse: Say: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah; indeed Allah forgives all sins and does not care; indeed He is the All-Forgiving, the Most Merciful."
"22080","Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Asma bint Yazid. 412 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hilal ibn Bishr narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Umarah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - mentioned the Dajjal and said: Before his emergence are three years in which the sky withholds a third of its rain and the earth a third of its vegetation. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"22081","Hammad ibn Ja'far Abu Ja'far al-Basri from Shahr. 413 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humran narrated to us, Marzuq Abu Abdullah al-Shami narrated to us, from Abi Ja'far, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: When you pray over the funeral, recite the Opening of the Book."
"22082","Hafs ibn Abi Hafs Abu Ma'mar al-Tamimi from Shahr. 414 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Thawban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Hafs ibn Abi Hafs Abu Ma'mar al-Tamimi narrated to us, he said: I heard Shahr ibn Hawshab narrating from Asma bint Yazid, she said: We were with the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - men and women, and he said: Perhaps a man speaks of what happens between him and his wife, or perhaps a woman speaks of what happens between her and her husband. The people fell silent. I said: Yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, they do that and they do that. He said: Do not do it, for the like of that is like a male devil meeting a female devil on the road and covering her while people look on."
"22083","415 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Hafs ibn Abi Hafs Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: We were with the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and he saw a woman wearing two gold bracelets. He said: Would it please you for Allah to encircle you with two bracelets of fire? So she removed them from her hand and threw them away, and I do not know who took them."
"22084","Budayl ibn Maysarah al-Uqayli from Shahr ibn Hawshab. 416 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The two sleeves of the shirt of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - reached below the wrists."
"22085","al-Hakam ibn Aban from Shahr ibn Hawshab. 417 - Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: I am among the women from whom the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - took the pledge. She said: I was a young, mature, bold girl in asking him, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, extend your hand so I may shake it. He said: I do not shake hands with women, but I take from them what Allah took from them. She said: He looked at a maternal aunt of mine wearing two gold bracelets, took something from the ground and threw it at her, saying: Would it please you for Allah to make for you two bracelets of the fire of Hell? She said: I seek refuge with Allah. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: If you have sought refuge with Allah, then cast these two off from you. She struggled with them and I helped her in that, and she cast them off; until this hour I do not know who took them."
"22086","418 - Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from his father, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, that while she was among women, the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - passed by them and greeted them, then said: Beware of the ingratitude of the blessed. She said: What is the ingratitude of the blessed, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Perhaps one of you remains long unmarried or stays unwed with her parents, then perhaps Allah provides her a husband, then provides her children from him, then she becomes angry and denies it, saying: By Allah, I have never seen any good from you at all."
"22087","Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym from Shahr ibn Hawshab. 419 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i narrated to us, my uncle Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - sent an expedition to the outskirts of Mudar. They mentioned that they camped in rocky land, and in the morning they found a man in his dome with sheep in his courtyard. They came until they stood before him and said: Shelter us. He sheltered them with a sheep and they cooked from it, then he brought out to them and they disliked it. Then he said: Nothing remains among my sheep of a meat sheep except a pregnant ewe or a stud. They clamored, and took a sheep from them. When they appeared and were scorched on a hot summer day with no shade with them, they said: His little sheep are in his shade. They said: We are more entitled to the shade than these sheep. They came to him and said: Remove your sheep from us so we may shade ourselves. He said: If you remove them they will perish and cast their young; I am a man who has believed in Allah and His Messenger, and I have prayed and paid zakah. They removed his sheep, and scarcely an hour of the day passed before they bleated in labor and cast their young. He set out quickly until he came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and informed him of the news. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - became intensely angry, then said: Sit until the people return. When they returned, he gathered them and him together, and they all cried out against him: Lie, lie. It was relieved from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. When the Bedouin saw that, he said: By Allah, Allah knows that I am truthful and they are liars; perhaps Allah will inform you, O Messenger of Allah. It occurred to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - that he was truthful, so he called them one by one, adjuring each man among them, and no man among them declared except as the Bedouin had said. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - stood and said: What carries you to follow one another in lying as moths follow one another into the fire? Lying is written against the son of Adam except in three traits: a man who lies to his wife so she is pleased with him, a man who lies in the deception of war, and a man who lies between two Muslim women to reconcile between them."
"22088","420 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, that she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: All lying is written against the son of Adam except in three: a man who lies in reconciling between people, or lies to his wife, or lies in the deception of war."
"22089","421 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, (ha). And Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, they both said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to me, Shahr ibn Hawshab al-Ash'ari narrated to us, from Asma bint Yazid al-Ansariyyah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - stood and addressed the people, saying: O people, what carries you to follow one another in lying - Zuhayr said: I think he said - as moths follow one another into the fire? All lying is written against the son of Adam except three traits: a man who lies to his wife to please her, or a man who lies between two Muslim women to reconcile between them, or a man who lies in the deception of war. And the wording is that of the hadith of Ahmad ibn Yunus."
"22090","422 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf and Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi' the two Egyptians narrated to us, they said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: O people, what carries you to follow one another in lying as moths follow one another into the fire? All lying is written against the son of Adam except three: a man who lies to his wife to please her, a man who lies between two to reconcile between them, and a man who lies in the deception of war."
"22091","423 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, (ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ka'bi narrated to us, they said: al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' al-Burani narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: O people, shall I not inform you of the best of you? They said: Yes. He said: Those who, when seen, Allah is remembered. Shall I not inform you of the worst of you? They said: Yes. He said: The worst of you are those who walk with tale-bearing, corrupt between loved ones, and seek affliction for the innocent."
"22092","424 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Shall I not inform you of the best of you? Then he mentioned the like of it."
"22093","425 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Shall I not inform you of the best of you? Then he mentioned the like of it."
"22094","426 - Khalaf ibn Dawud al-Ukbari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - went out to the women in the side of the mosque, and I was with them. He heard their voices and said: O company of women, you are the most of the firewood of Hell. I called out to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while I was bold in speaking to him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, why? He said: Because when you are given you are not grateful, when you are tried you are not patient, and when withheld from you complain; beware of the ingratitude of the blessed. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the ingratitude of the blessed? He said: A woman is with a man and has borne him two or three children, then she says: I have never seen any good from you at all."
"22095","427 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i narrated to us, my uncle Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - the like of it."
"22096","428 - Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ka'bi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Whoever drinks wine, Allah will not be pleased with him for forty days; if he dies he dies a disbeliever, if he repents Allah turns to him, and if he returns it will be incumbent upon Allah to give him to drink of the mud of khabal. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the mud of khabal? He said: The pus of the people of the Fire."
"22097","429 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Whoever drinks wine, Allah will not be pleased with him for forty mornings; if he dies he dies a disbeliever, if he repents Allah turns to him, and if he returns it will be incumbent upon Allah to give him to drink of the mud of khabal on the Day of Resurrection. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the mud of khabal? He said: The pus of the people of the Fire."
"22098","430 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - among his Companions say: I warn you of the Masih and caution you against him; every prophet warned his people, and he is among you, O ummah. I will describe to you of his description what the prophets before me did not describe to their peoples: before his emergence are five barren years until every hoofed one perishes. A man called out to him: O Messenger of Allah, on what will the believers live? He said: On what the angels live. Then he emerges, one-eyed, while Allah is not one-eyed; between his eyes is written disbeliever, which every believer, literate and illiterate, will read. Most who follow him are Jews, women and Bedouins. They see the sky raining while it does not rain, and the earth sprouting while it does not sprout. He says to the Bedouins: What do you seek from me? Did I not send the sky upon you pouring, and revive your livestock for you with prominent udders, protruding flanks and flowing milk? Devils are sent with him in the form of those who died among fathers, brothers and acquaintances; one of them comes to his father or brother or kin and says: Am I not so-and-so? Do you not recognize me? He is your lord, so follow him. He lives forty years: the first year like a month, the month like a Friday, the Friday like a day, the day like an hour, and the hour like the burning of a palm frond in fire. He comes to every watering place except the two mosques. Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - stood to perform ablution, heard the weeping and sobbing of the people, returned to them and stood among them, saying: Rejoice; if he emerges while I am among you, Allah and His Messenger suffice you; if he emerges after me, Allah is my deputy over every Muslim."
"22099","431 - Ishaq ibn Jamil al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: I and my maternal aunt entered upon the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - wearing two gold bracelets. He said: Do you pay their zakah? We said: No. He said: Would you love for Allah to encircle you with two bracelets of fire? Pay their zakah."
"22100","432 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: When Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - died, the eyes of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - shed tears. It was said to him: You are the most entitled to know the right of Allah. He said: The eye weeps, the heart grieves, and we do not say what angers the Lord. Were it not that it is a true promise, a gathering appointment, and that the last follows the first, we would grieve more than this; O Ibrahim, we are grieved for you."
"22101","433 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i narrated to us, my uncle Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, that Asma bint Yazid said: When Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - died, the one consoling him - either Abu Bakr or Umar - said: You know best the right of Allah. He said: The eye weeps, the heart grieves, and we do not say what angers the Lord. Were it not that it is a true promise, a gathering appointment, and that the last follows the first, we would feel for you, O Ibrahim, more than we feel; O Ibrahim, we are grieved for you."
"22102","Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn al-Makki from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Asma bint Yazid. 434 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: I am the one who adorned A'ishah for the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. When I presented her to him and brought her to him, I seated her at his right. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was brought a cup of milk and drank, then handed it to A'ishah, but she lowered her head and felt shy. I said to her: Take from the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. So she took and drank. Then he said: Hand it to your companion. She said: O Messenger of Allah, drink yourself. Then he handed it to me and drank, then handed it to me, and I began to follow the places of the lips of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while women were near us - or with us. He said: Hand it to your companions. They said: We do not desire it - or: we do not want it. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Do not combine lying and hunger. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saw upon one of us a gold bracelet and said: O you, would you love for Allah to encircle you in its place with a bracelet of fire? So we removed it and threw it away, and until this hour we do not know where it is. Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: It suffices one of you to take beads of silver - perhaps he said: a bracelet of silver - then take some saffron, dissolve it, then smear it over it, and it looks as though it were gold."
"22103","435 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Nashit, from Ibn Abi Husayn, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, that she was with the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and a large cup of milk was brought. He drank from it, then said: Give them - to women with him. They said: We do not desire it. He said: Do not combine lying and hunger."
"22104","436 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, (ha). And Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, they both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - passed by me while I was among women and greeted us, saying: Beware of the ingratitude of the blessed. I said: What is the ingratitude of the blessed? He said: Perhaps one of you remains long unmarried among her parents and stays unwed, then Allah provides her a husband and provides her wealth and children from him, then she becomes angry and denies it, saying: I have never seen any good from you at all."
"22105","437 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to her while she was among women and we said: Take our pledge, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I do not shake hands with you, but I take from you what Allah took from them."
"22106","438 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Husayn, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - spoke to us one day about the Dajjal. A woman stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, I knead the dough of my family and I think my soul will depart before it is done. He said: If he emerges while I am among you, I will dispute against him; if he emerges after me, Allah is my deputy over every Muslim."
"22107","439 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn Abi Husayn narrated to me, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: I heard the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: There was no prophet except that he warned his ummah of the Dajjal, and I caution you against him."
"22108","Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qaddah from Shahr ibn Hawshab. 440 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The Greatest Name of Allah is in these two verses: Alif Lam Mim. Allah, there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer; and: Your god is one God."
"22109","441 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (ha). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, they both said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The Greatest Name of Allah is in these two verses: Your god is one God; and: Alif Lam Mim. Allah, there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer."
"22110","442 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever defends the flesh of his brother in absence, it is incumbent upon Allah to shield him from the Fire."
"22111","443 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - he said: Whoever defends the honor of his brother in absence, it is incumbent upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to free him from the Fire."
"22112","Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram from Shahr. 444 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, Asma bint Yazid narrated to me, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - died on the day he died while his armor was pawned with a Jewish man for a wasq of barley."
"22113","445 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, he said: I heard Asma bint Yazid say: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered the mosque one day while a group of women were sitting. He waved his right hand in salam and smiled at them, saying: Beware of the ingratitude of the blessed. A woman said: I seek refuge with Allah, O Messenger of Allah, from ingratitude for the blessings of Allah. He said: One of you remains long unmarried, then Allah provides her a husband, and she gains children and the coolness of the eye, then she becomes angry and swears by Allah: I have never seen an hour of good from him at all. That is from ingratitude for the blessings of Allah, that is from ingratitude for the blessings of Allah, that is from ingratitude for the blessings of Allah."
"22114","446 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - sat in a gathering and warned them of the Dajjal, then he mentioned the hadith."
"22115","Layth ibn Abi Sulaym from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Asma. 447 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzar narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - recite: Woe to your mother, Quraysh, for your accustomed journey of winter and summer."
"22116","448 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: I was holding the rein of al-Adba, the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - when al-Ma'idah was revealed upon him, and from its weight it almost broke the neck of the she-camel."
"22117","449 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: al-An'am was revealed upon the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - all at once, while I was holding the rein of the she-camel of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -; from its weight it almost broke the bone of the she-camel."
"22118","450 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to me, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - the like of it."
"22119","451 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon me while I wore gold rings and a gold bracelet. He said: Would it please you for Allah to seal you with a ring of fire and encircle you with a bracelet of fire? So I left it. And he said: Is one of you unable to take a ring of silver and smear upon it saffron, amber and wars?"
"22120","452 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, (ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, both from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: We were with the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - one day when a drink was brought. He drank, then gave the people and they drank. The vessel passed by a man among the people who said: I am fasting. One of the people said: He does not break fast; he fasts every day. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: He neither fasted nor broke fast who fasts perpetually."
"22121","453 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was brought a drink, and it went around the people, among them a fasting man. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, he fasts perpetually. He said: He who fasts perpetually has not fasted."
"22122","454 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from his father, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - he said: He who fasts perpetually has not fasted."
"22123","Mustaqim ibn Abd al-Malik from Shahr from Asma. 455 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah al-Kilabi narrated to us, Mustaqim ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would not shake hands with women."
"22124","al-Miqdam ibn Abi al-Miqdam, whose name of Abi al-Miqdam is Thabit, from Shahr from Asma. 456 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, they both said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Abi al-Miqdam al-Haddad, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: I came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - I and a cousin of mine to pledge to him. He said: I do not shake hands with women."
"22125","Yazid Abu Abdullah al-Shaybani from Shahr from Asma. 457 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn and Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, they said: Yazid Abu Abdullah al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: I heard Shahr ibn Hawshab say: Umm Salamah al-Ansariyyah narrated to us that she was among the women from whom the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - took what he took, and with her was her maternal aunt wearing gold rings and two gold bracelets. He kept turning his gaze away from her until, when he finished, he said: What is this? Would it please you for Allah to adorn you with adornment of fire? She said: I seek refuge with Allah from the Fire. She removed her rings and threw them before her, struggled with her bracelets but could not, so she set to them and bit them off from her, throwing them in a place we do not know what became of. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we women must beautify ourselves for our husbands, so permit us two earrings of gold. He refused me, saying: It suffices one of you to take two earrings of silver, then take two hairs of saffron and pass them between her fingers, then yellow it, and it looks like gold."
"22126","458 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Yazid al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: I heard Shahr ibn Hawshab say: Umm Salamah al-Ansariyyah narrated to me that a woman among the women said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this good for which we were forbidden to disobey you? He said: Do not wail. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the sons of so-and-so helped me over my cousin so-and-so's daughter, and I must repay them. He refused me, then I repeated it several times, and he permitted me to repay them; I have not wailed since repaying them, nor other than it, until this hour, and none of the women remains but has wailed except me."
"22127","Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Shaybani from Shahr from Asma, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. 459 - Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Shaybani narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me that he met Asma bint Yazid, he said: She narrated to me that she pledged to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - on the day he pledged the women. She leaned and extended her hand to pledge him, but he withheld his hand and said: I do not shake hands with women; I only take from them in word. She said: I wore a garment and jewelry. He said: O Asma. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and joy to you. He said: Would it please you to be branded with this jewelry? I said: What is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Whoever adorns herself with gold or adorns one of her children with the like of a small earring or a locust's leg will be branded with it on the Day of Resurrection."
"22128","Abu Tahir al-Kufi from Shahr ibn Hawshab. 460 - Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Abi Tahir, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, he said: Asma bint Yazid narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - died while his armor with which he fought was pawned for a wasq of barley with a Jewish man, which he took as food for his family."
"22129","Mujahid from Asma. 461 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (ha). And Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Urwah narrated to us, they both said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Ajlan, from Mujahid, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said concerning the aqiqah: For the boy two sheep, and for the girl one sheep."
"22130","al-Muhajir al-Ansari from Asma bint Yazid. 462 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Muhajir, that he heard his father narrating from Asma bint Yazid - and she was his freedwoman - that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Do not kill your children secretly; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, ghayl overtakes the horseman on the back of his horse until it throws him down."
"22131","463 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muhajir al-Ansari, from his father, from Asma bint Yazid al-Ansariyyah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Do not kill your children secretly, for the one who commits ghayl overtakes the horseman and throws him from the back of his horse."
"22132","464 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muhajir al-Ansari, from his father, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - passed by me while I was among young girls of my age, saying: Beware of the ingratitude of the blessed. I was bolder than others in asking him, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the ingratitude of the blessed? He said: Perhaps one of you remains long unmarried with her parents, then Allah provides her a husband and provides her children, then she becomes angry and denies it, saying: By Allah, I have never seen any good from you at all."
"22133","465 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from his father, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever leaves two dinars leaves two brands."
"22134","466 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from his father, he said: Asma bint Yazid narrated to us, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was called to the funeral of a man of the Ansar. When the bier was placed, the Prophet of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - stepped forward to pray over him, then turned and said: Is there a debt upon your companion? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, two dinars. He said: Pray over your companion. Abu Qatadah said: We owe it, O Prophet of Allah. So he prayed over him."
"22135","Ishaq ibn Rashid from Asma bint Yazid. 467 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they both said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Ishaq ibn Khalid, from a woman of the Ansar called Asma bint Yazid ibn al-Sakan, she said: When the funeral of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh was brought out, his mother cried out. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to her: Let your tears dry and your grief depart, for your son is the first at whom Allah laughed and for whom the Throne shook."
"22136","Mahmud ibn Amr from Asma. 468 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Mahmud ibn Amr, from Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise."
"22137","469 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastawa'i, from Mahmud ibn Amr, from Asma bint Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Any woman who adorns herself with a necklace of gold, the like of it of fire will be placed around her neck on the Day of Resurrection."
"22138","Those named Umaymah. Umaymah bint Ruqayqah al-Taymiyyah. 470 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: Umaymah bint Ruqayqah informed me, she said: I came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - with women to pledge him, and he stipulated upon us what is in the Qur'an: Do not steal, do not commit adultery, do not kill your children, and do not come with slander you fabricate. Then he said to us: In what you are able and can bear. We said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than ourselves. We said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not shake hands with us? He said: I do not shake hands with women; my word to a woman is like my word to a hundred women."
"22139","471 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, (ha). And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, (ha). And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Umaymah bint Ruqayqah, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - with women to pledge him. We said: We pledge you, O Messenger of Allah, that we will not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery, nor kill our children, nor come with slander we fabricate between our hands and feet, nor disobey you in good. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: In what you are able and can bear. We said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than ourselves; come, let us pledge you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I do not shake hands with women; my word to a hundred women is like my word to a single woman, or like my word to a single woman."
"22140","472 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, (ha). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Umaymah bint Ruqayqah, she said: I came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - with women, and he said: You pledge that you will not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery - the verse - then he said: In what you are able and can bear. We said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than ourselves. We said: O Messenger of Allah, pledge us. He said: I do not shake hands with women; my word to a hundred women among you is like my word to a single woman."
"22141","473 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to him, that Umaymah bint Ruqayqah al-Taymiyyah narrated to him, that she came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - with women, and he said: You pledge that you will not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery - the verse - then he fell silent, then said: In what you are able and can bear. We said: Allah and His Messenger know better and are more merciful to us than ourselves. We said: O Messenger of Allah, pledge us. He said: I do not shake hands with women; my word to a hundred women is like my word to a single woman."
"22142","474 - al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Janadi narrated to us, Ali ibn Ziyad al-Lahji narrated to us, Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah ibn Salih mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, that he heard Umaymah bint Ruqayqah say: She pledged the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -, and he stipulated upon her what he stipulated upon the believing women, then said: In what you can bear."
"22143","475 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, that he heard Umaymah bint Ruqayqah claim that she pledged the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -, and he stipulated upon her what he stipulated upon the believing women in the Book of Allah, then said: In what you can bear, O daughter of Ruqayqah."
"22144","476 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja al-Ghudani narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Umaymah bint Ruqayqah al-Taymiyyah, she said: I entered upon the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - with women, and we said: We pledge you, O Messenger of Allah, that we will not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery, nor come with slander we fabricate between our hands and feet, nor disobey you in good. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: In what you can bear and are able. We said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us; pledge us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I do not shake hands with women; my word to a hundred is like my word to one."
"22145","Umaymah bint Ruqayqah bint Sayfi ibn Hashim ibn Abd Manaf. 477 - Ahmad ibn Ziyad al-Hadhdha al-Raqqi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hakimah bint Umaymah bint Ruqayqah narrated to me, from her mother, that she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would urinate in a wooden cup, then place it under his bed. He urinated in it, then came seeking it, and the cup had nothing in it. He said to a woman called Barakah, who used to serve Umm Habibah and had been brought with her from the land of Abyssinia: Where is the urine that was in the cup? She said: I drank it. He said: You have protected yourself from the Fire with a protection."
"22146","478 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hukaymah informed me, from her mother Umaymah, that the wives of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would make a band containing wars and saffron and bind with it the lower ends of their hair at their foreheads before entering ihram, then enter ihram likewise."
"22147","Umaymah, freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. 479 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, (ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, both from Yazid ibn Sinan, from Sulaym ibn Amir Abi Yahya, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Umaymah, freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -, she said: I used to pour the ablution water of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. A man entered and said: Advise me. He said: Do not associate anything with Allah, even if you are cut and burned with fire; do not disobey your parents, even if they order you to abandon your family and your world, then abandon it; do not drink wine, for it is the head of all evil; do not abandon prayer deliberately, for whoever does that, the protection of Allah and His Messenger is free of him; do not flee on the day of battle, for whoever does that returns with anger from Allah, and his abode is Hell, an evil destination; do not encroach upon the boundaries of your land, for whoever does that will come with it upon his neck on the Day of Resurrection to the extent of seven earths; spend upon your family from your means; do not lift your stick from them; and frighten them concerning Allah."
"22148","Those named Unaysah. Unaysah bint Khubayb. 480 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, (ha). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, they both said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard my paternal aunt, who had performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -, say: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Bilal calls the adhan, or Ibn Umm Maktum. One of them would ascend and the other descend, and we would cling to him saying: Stay as you are until we take sahur."
"22149","481 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his paternal aunt Unaysah, who was a praying woman, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - he said: Ibn Umm Maktum or Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Bilal or Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan. One of them would hardly call the adhan before the other ascended, so we would take him by his hand and say: Stay as you are until we take sahur."
"22150","482 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, from Mansur, from Zadham, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Khubayb, from his paternal aunt Unaysah bint Khubayb, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: When Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan, eat and drink until Bilal calls the adhan. When anything of her sahur remained for one of us, she would say: O Bilal, hold back until we finish our sahur."
"22151","Unaysah bint Adi. 483 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Janab al-Missisi narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Uthman al-Balawi, from his grandmother Unaysah bint Adi, that she came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: O Messenger of Allah, my son Abdullah ibn Salamah - and he was a Badr veteran - was killed on the day of Uhud; I wished to move him so I may find comfort in his nearness. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - permitted her. She balanced him with al-Mijdhar ibn Ziyad on a water-carrying camel of his in an aba'ah. She passed with them, and the people marveled at them. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - looked at them and said: Their deeds made them equal. Abdullah was a bulky, heavy man, while al-Mijdhar was lean-fleshed; he is the one who says: With the spear he pierces."
"22152","Chapter of Ba. Busrah bint Safwan ibn Nawfal ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Qusayy, maternal aunt of Marwan ibn al-Hakam, grandmother of Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan. 484 - Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Ma'n ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that Busrah bint Safwan asked the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - about a woman who strikes with her hand and touches her private part. He said: Perform ablution, O Busrah."
"22153","485 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: He and Marwan discussed ablution from touching the private part. Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan narrated to me that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - command ablution from touching the private part. Urwah seemingly did not value his hadith, so Marwan sent a policeman to her; he returned and informed them that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - command ablution from touching the private part."
"22154","486 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Namir al-Yahsabi narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, that he heard Marwan say: Busrah bint Safwan informed me, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution."
"22155","487 - Abu Shu'ayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to me, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Busrah bint Safwan, that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: A man performs ablution from touching the male organ."
"22156","488 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm informed me, from Urwah, from Busrah bint Safwan, that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Whoever touches his male organ, let him perform ablution."
"22157","489 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Kilabi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from Ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, that Urwah narrated to him, that Marwan mentioned, that Busrah bint Safwan said: She heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution."
"22158","490 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, from al-Layth ibn Sa'd, (ha). And Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, that he said: Ablution is from touching the male organ. Urwah denied that, so Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan informed me of it. He sent to Busrah, and she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - mentioned what ablution is performed from, and mentioned touching the male organ."
"22159","491 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Urwah, that he used to narrate from Busrah bint Safwan, or from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: When one of you touches his male organ, let him perform ablution."
"22160","492 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm al-Ansari, that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr say: Marwan ibn al-Hakam mentioned during his governorship over Madinah that ablution is performed from touching the male organ when a man lays his hand upon it. I denied that, saying: There is no ablution from touching it. Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - mention what ablution is performed from. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Ablution is performed from touching the male organ. Urwah said: I kept disputing with Marwan about that until he called a man of his guard and sent him to Busrah bint Safwan, asking her about what she narrated to him of that; Busrah sent back the like of what Marwan had narrated to me from her."
"22161","493 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn al-Buhturi al-Ta'i narrated to us, Bishr ibn Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from his father, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr say: Marwan mentioned that ablution is performed from touching the male organ when a man lays his hand upon it. I denied that, saying: There is no ablution upon one who touches it. Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - mention what ablution is performed from. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: And ablution is performed from touching the male organ. Urwah said: I kept disputing with Marwan until he called a man of his guard and sent him to Busrah to ask her about what he narrated of that; Busrah sent back to him the like of what he had narrated to me from him."
"22162","494 - Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating from Marwan, from Busrah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever touches his male organ, let him perform ablution."
"22163","495 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-San'ani narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating from Marwan, from Busrah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever touches his male organ, let him perform ablution."
"22164","496 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, (ha). And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Malik informed us, (ha). And Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr say: I entered upon Marwan ibn al-Hakam, and he mentioned what ablution results from. Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan informed me that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever touches his male organ, let him perform ablution."
"22165","497 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Busrah bint Safwan, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever touches his male organ, let him perform ablution."
"22166","498 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-San'ani narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad al-Umari, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Busrah bint Safwan, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - he said: A man performs ablution from touching the male organ."
"22167","499 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin and Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf, the two Egyptians, narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, he narrated to him: from Urwah, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, from Busrah bint Safwan, she said: What ablution is performed from was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -, and he said: And whoever touches the male organ performs ablution."
"22168","500 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, he said: I heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating to my father, he said: Marwan discussed with me touching the male organ. I said: There is no ablution from it. He said: Busrah bint Safwan narrates concerning it. He sent a messenger to her, and he mentioned that she narrated to him that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution."
"22169","501 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Urwah, from Marwan, from Busrah bint Safwan, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever touches his male organ, let him perform ablution."
"22170","502 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Khalaf Abu Salamah al-Jawbari narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Urwah, from Marwan, from Busrah bint Safwan, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever touches his male organ, let him perform ablution."
"22171","503 - Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sufyan al-Jahdari narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to us, he said: I heard Urwah say: Marwan sent to Busrah and asked her about this hadith; she narrated that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: When one of you touches his male organ, let him perform ablution."
"22172","504 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm informed me, from Urwah, from Busrah bint Safwan, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Whoever touches his private part, let him not pray until he performs ablution."
"22173","505 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Busrah bint Safwan, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: When one of you touches his male organ, let him perform ablution."
"22174","506 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: Marwan ibn al-Hakam informed me, from Busrah bint Safwan, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: When one of you touches his private part, let him perform ablution. He said: So I objected to him, and he sent to her; she narrated to him from the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while I was present."
"22175","507 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, that he was with Marwan ibn al-Hakam when asked about touching the male organ, and he saw no harm in it. Marwan sent one of his guard to Busrah bint Safwan, saying: She narrated to me that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: When a man touches his private part with his hand, let him not pray until he performs ablution. He returned and said: She said: Yes. After that my father used to say: Whoever touches his groin, testicles or male organ, let him perform ablution."
"22176","508 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Marwan, from Busrah bint Safwan, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: When one of you touches his male organ, let him perform ablution."
"22177","509 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that Marwan ibn al-Hakam said: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution. Urwah objected to him, saying: O policeman, go to Busrah bint Safwan and ask her; she said: I heard the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Whoever touches his male organ, let him perform ablution."
"22178","510 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Busrah bint Safwan, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: When one of you touches his male organ, testicles or groin, let him perform ablution."
"22179","511 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ali ibn Muslim al-Tusi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Busrah bint Safwan, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Whoever touches his male organ, testicles or groin, let him perform ablution, his ablution for prayer."
"22180","512 - Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: I was with Marwan ibn al-Hakam when asked about touching the male organ, and I did not see renewal of ablution upon it. Marwan called one of his police and sent him to Busrah bint Safwan, asking her about that; she informed him that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: When one of you touches his male organ, let him renew ablution."
"22181","513 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya, scribe of al-Umari, narrated to us, Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, from Busrah bint Safwan, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever touches his male organ or testicles, let him perform ablution."
"22182","514 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, from Busrah bint Safwan, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever touches his male organ, let him perform ablution, his ablution for prayer."
"22183","515 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Marwan, from Busrah bint Safwan, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever touches his private part, ablution is obligatory upon him."
"22184","516 - Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Busrah bint Safwan, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever touches his groin, testicles or male organ, let him not pray until he performs ablution."
"22185","517 - Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Dashtaki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Uthman, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, from Busrah bint Safwan al-Asadiyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever touches his male organ, let him perform ablution. Urwah said: So I asked Busrah and she confirmed him."
"22186","518 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Busrah bint Safwan, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: When one of you touches his penis, let him perform ablution. 519 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Shu'bah said: Hisham did not hear the hadith of his father about touching the penis. Yahya said: So I asked Hisham and he said: My father informed me."
"22187","520 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Marwan, from Busrah bint Safwan, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: When one of you touches his penis, let him perform ablution."
"22188","521 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Busrah bint Safwan al-Kinaniyyah, and she was the maternal aunt of Marwan, she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: O Messenger of Allah, is ablution obligatory upon one of us when she touches her private part? So the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever among men and women touches his private part, ablution is obligatory upon him."
"22189","Those whose name is Buqayrah. Buqayrah, the wife of al-Qa'qa' ibn Abi Hadrad al-Ansari. 522 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Buqayrah, the wife of al-Qa'qa' ibn Abi Hadrad, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: O you people, when you hear of an army nearby that has been swallowed up by the earth, then the Hour has cast its shadow over you."
"22190","523 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated to us, (H) and Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Masayrah al-Razi narrated to us, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, both of them, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Ata, from Buqayrah, the wife of al-Qa'qa', she said: I was sitting in the women's suffah when I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: O people, when you hear of a swallowing of the earth nearby here, then the Hour has cast its shadow over you."
"22191","Buthaynah bint al-Dahhak al-Ansariyyah. 524 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr saying: Buthaynah bint al-Dahhak is the sister of Thabit, and she is the one whom Muhammad ibn Maslamah proposed to."
"22192","Barirah, the mukatabah of A'ishah, the Mother of the Believers, wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. 525 - Abu Yazid Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Barirah, she said: Three matters of the Sunnah occurred in my case: meat was given to me in charity and I gifted it to A'ishah, and she kept it until the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered and said: What is this meat? She said: Meat given in charity to Barirah, and she gifted it to us. He said: It is charity for Barirah and a gift for us. She said: And I contracted kitabah for nine awaq, and A'ishah said: If they wish, I will count it out for them in one payment. I said: They say: Unless wala' is stipulated for them. So the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Stipulate, and stipulate a condition, for wala' belongs to the one who frees. She said: And I was freed, and I had the choice."
"22193","526 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abd al-Khaliq ibn Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to us, my father narrated to me that Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan narrated to them, he said: I used to sit with Barirah in Madinah before I assumed this authority, and she used to say: O Abd al-Malik, I see in you qualities; you are surely fit to rule this ummah. If you are put in charge of it, then beware of blood, for I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: A man will be pushed back from the gate of Paradise, prevented from looking at it, on account of a cupping-glassful of blood he shed from a Muslim without right."
"22194","Barrah, the servant of Umm Salamah, the Mother of the Believers. 527 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Hakimah bint Umaymah, from her mother Umaymah, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - had a vessel made of wood in which he would urinate, and he would place it under his bed. He got up and looked for it but did not find it, so he asked and said: Where is the vessel? They said: Barrah, the servant of Umm Salamah who came with her from the land of Abyssinia, drank it. So the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: She has surely protected herself from the Fire with a protection."
"22195","Buhaysah. 528 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Sayyar ibn Manzur, from his father, from a woman of theirs called Buhaysah, she said: My father sought permission from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - to enter between him and his shirt, so he permitted him. He entered between him and his shirt from behind and began to embrace him and wipe his chest against the back of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is it that is not lawful to withhold? He said: Water. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is it that is not lawful to withhold? He said: Salt. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is it that is not lawful to withhold? He said: To do good is better for you. His statement ended at water and salt. She said: That man would not withhold anything of water, even if little."
"22196","The chapter of Ta'. Tamluk. 529 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, Mihran ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Hakim, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Tamluk, she said: I looked at the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while I was in a room of mine between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and he was saying: Allah has prescribed sa'y upon you, so perform sa'y."
"22197","Tuwaylah bint Aslam. 530 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Ja'far ibn Mahmud ibn Maslamah al-Harithi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandmother, the mother of his father Tuwaylah bint Aslam, and she was among the women who gave pledge, she said: While we were at our place praying in Banu Harithah, Abbad ibn Bishr ibn Qayzi said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - has faced the Sacred House, or the Ka'bah. So the men moved to the place of the women, and the women to the place of the men, and they prayed the remaining two rak'ahs toward the Ka'bah."
"22198","Al-Taw'amah bint Umayyah ibn Khalaf: she is mentioned, and she has no hadith. 531 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam ibn Abi Ziyad saying: Salih is the freedman of al-Taw'amah, and she is the daughter of Umayyah ibn Khalaf."
"22199","The chapter of Jim. Jahdamah, the wife of Bashir ibn al-Khassasiyyah. 532 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sawaa' narrated to us, from Abu Janab al-Kalbi Yahya ibn Abi Hayyah, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Jahdamah, the wife of Bashir ibn al-Khassasiyyah, she said: The name of Bashir was Zahm, so the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - named him Bashir."
"22200","533 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Dahiri narrated to us, from Abu Janab al-Kalbi, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from al-Jahdamah, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - come out to prayer shaking his head and his beard from the traces of henna."
